#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cloud-tests: run a project's test suites in a Claude Code cloud session instead of the laptop's heavy-job slots.

Supervisors send the test suites to cloud sessions, unattended, so the machine's heavy-job slots stay free; each
project keeps its cloud setup in the repository so a new cloud session starts fast; no redundant test sessions or runs.

How it works (all from Bash, so it also works in a supervisor's automated tick, where the app refuses start_session):
  * One runner per project: a cloud session created with `claude --cloud` (through a pseudo-terminal, the CLI needs a
    TTY). Requests reach it as follow-ups (`claude -p <msg> --cloud <session>`), ONE AT A TIME: the queue lives in the
    ledger (state `queued`), not in the runner. Whoever calls request, poll, wait or pump (under the ledger lock) sends
    the oldest queued run when the runner is free (`dispatch`), so a queued run can be superseded or expired, and a
    silent runner is noticed: a dispatched run past its deadline marks the runner dead, goes back to the head of the
    queue once and a fresh runner is launched; the second time it expires. If the launch fails, the head run expires
    (`launch_failed`) and no launch is tried again for LAUNCH_BACKOFF_S. The deadline counts from the dispatch, not from
    the request. A queued run never sent within QUEUE_MAX_S expires.
  * A runner remembers the brief version and the digest of the runner kit it was launched with (`brief_version`,
    `kit_sha`). One launched with an older brief or another kit (or without the fields) is not given new runs: the next
    dispatch launches a fresh runner and `sweep` retires the old one.
  * The runner kit (lib/cloud_tests_kit.py, embedded verbatim at the end of the brief) runs each request in one process
    with hooks that record every test (a pytest plugin by entry point, a jest preload, else JUnit files) and writes
    runs/<run>.tests.tsv; no environment has to survive between the runner's own tool calls.
  * A newer request for the same suite and branch supersedes the older runs still queued (SUPERSEDED); `wait` follows
    the chain to the successor. Runs already sent cannot be cancelled.
  * `pump` (hidden, spawned detached by request while runs are queued or sent) keeps polling so the queue moves with
    nobody waiting; one per project (flock), it stops when nothing is queued or sent.
  * `preflight` (top level of the recipe, or per suite): check-only shell commands run locally, under heavy-job
    `--kind typecheck`, before queuing, when the checkout is exactly the pushed tree. A failure is PREFLIGHT_FAILED
    (exit 6) and nothing is queued: it saves a runner slot for code that cannot pass (style, lint, static analysis).
  * The runner checks out the exact pushed commit, runs the suite command from the project's recipe
    (`.claude/cloud-tests.json`, committed) and publishes the result as `runs/<run>.json` on the branch
    `cloud-tests-results` (commit message with `[skip ci]`). A cloud session cannot message back and the app does not
    list sessions created by the CLI, so git is the return channel.
  * A machine-wide ledger (~/.claude/state/cloud-tests/<project key>.json, flock) dedupes: the same tree and command
    is never run twice. A finished one is reused (REUSE), one in flight is waited for (WAIT).
  * The account's usage limit (2026-11-19) is not a mute runner. While the account the CLI launches cloud sessions with
    is out of usage (usage endpoint; refused desktop turns when it does not answer), nothing is launched, sent or
    expired and no deadline runs: runs wait QUEUED with `held_by_limit_until=HH:MM`. When it ends, a run that was in
    the cloud during it gets a whole new deadline from the end of the limit (plus LIMIT_RESUME_GRACE_MIN): a cut
    session may carry on by itself. If it stays silent past that, it is a mute runner as usual. The queue clock starts
    again at the end of the limit, and the pump stays alive until after a long limit.
  * A run that expires (deadline twice, launch failure, or too long in the queue) is EXPIRED: the caller runs it locally
    with heavy-job and records it with `record-local`.
  * No redundant local run: a suite that runs in the cloud is not run locally too, and a local copy already running
    or queued is stopped:
      - `heavy-job run|hold` asks `local-guard` first and refuses (exit 76) a suite that is in flight in the cloud, or
        already green there (24 h), for the same code: same project, same command (the recipe's `command`, its
        `local_commands` and the command in `equivalent_to`, leading VAR=value dropped) and the same tree (the tree of
        the working directory, uncommitted and untracked files included);
      - when a run is SENT, WAITed for or REUSEd green, and on every poll of `wait`, the same local jobs that were
        already running or queued in heavy-job are stopped: the wrapper's whole process tree and, for `ddev exec` /
        `docker exec`, the matching exec in the container. The wrapper prints why and exits 76.

Commands (run inside the project's checkout or a worktree of it, or pass --repo):
  check                         ELIGIBLE <owner/name> (exit 0) or LOCAL <reason> (exit 3)
  request --suite S [--ref BR] [--skip-preflight]
                                SENT|QUEUED|WAIT|REUSE <run> ... (exit 0); LOCAL (3); NOT_PUSHED (4); LAUNCH_FAILED (5);
                                PREFLIGHT_FAILED (6: fix the code and request again, never run the suite locally because
                                of it). Run states: queued sent done local expired mismatch superseded
  poll                          DONE / PENDING / QUEUED / EXPIRED lines for the runs of the last 24 h (moves the queue)
  wait RUN [RUN...]             polls until they finish: 0 all done, 5 one expired, 75 timeout (run in background);
                                follows SUPERSEDED runs to their successor
  result RUN [--tests [--grep RE]]
                                the stored result, JSON; with --tests the per-test lines (`outcome<TAB>id`) the runner
                                published in `runs/<run>.tests.tsv` on the results branch, filtered by the regex RE
                                (exit 3 when the run published none)
  record-local --suite S --exit N --summary TEXT [--ref BR]   a local fallback run, so others reuse it
  status                        runner and runs
  runner [--forget]             show or drop the project's runner
  local-guard [--cwd D] -- CMD  exit 3 + why when CMD here is redundant with a cloud run (heavy-job calls it), else 0
  stop-local [RUN...]           stop the redundant local jobs of these runs (of all in-flight runs without RUN)
  brief                         the runner brief (what the cloud session is told; BRIEF_VERSION says which one)
  pump                          (hidden) keeps the queue moving until nothing is queued or sent
  sweep [--dry-run]             archives in the cloud the runners of every project that nobody needs any more: replaced,
                                used up or failed, idle and quiet for 3 h, no run waiting (the supervisor-watchdog timer
                                runs it every 10 min; ARCHIVED / WOULD_ARCHIVE / SKIP / WARN lines, always exit 0)
  self-test                     offline tests with a fake `claude` and a local origin

Configuration (toolkit piece `cloud-tests`, ~/.claude/toolkit/config/cloud-tests.json; a missing or wrong value keeps
the default, a broken file never raises):
  excluded_names   repository or checkout names whose code never goes to the cloud (default: none)
  excluded_owners  GitHub owners whose repositories never go to the cloud (default: none)

Optional pieces: heavy-job (preflight and the redundant-local-run guard; without it the preflight is skipped and
nothing local is stopped), account-switch (the account's usage limit; without it the account is never taken for
limited) and supervisor-lock (the project key; without it the key is the checkout name plus a hash).
"""
import argparse
import contextlib
import fcntl
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import shlex
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time

STATE_DIR = os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_STATE', os.path.expanduser('~/.claude/state/cloud-tests'))
RECIPE = '.claude/cloud-tests.json'
RESULTS_BRANCH = 'cloud-tests-results'
RESULTS_LOCAL_REF = 'refs/cloud-tests/results'
BRIEF_VERSION = 3  # 3: the request runs through the kit; 2: JUnit -> runs/<run>.tests.tsv; a lower one is not reused
KIT_FILE = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), 'lib', 'cloud_tests_kit.py')
KIT_BEGIN = '-----BEGIN CLOUD-TESTS-KIT-----'
KIT_END = '-----END CLOUD-TESTS-KIT-----'
TESTS_FILE_MAX_LINES = 50000
MAX_RUNS_PER_RUNNER = int(os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_MAX_RUNS', '15'))
MAX_RUNNER_AGE_S = int(os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_MAX_RUNNER_AGE_S', str(3 * 86400)))
DEFAULT_DEADLINE_MIN = 60
LAUNCH_OVERHEAD_MIN = 15  # cloud VM start, setup hook and checkout before the suite starts
DISPATCH_OVERHEAD_MIN = 5  # a follow-up to a running runner: checkout and setup before the suite starts
LAUNCH_BACKOFF_S = 600  # after a failed launch, no new launch is tried for this long
QUEUE_MAX_S = 3 * 3600  # a run still queued after this long expires (the runner never became free)
PREFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_S = 20 * 60
PUMP_MAX_S = 8 * 3600
RETRYABLE_EXITS = (97, 98)  # the cloud could not run the suite, or its result was unreadable: never reused
HEAVY_JOB_BIN = os.environ.get('HEAVY_JOB_BIN', os.path.expanduser('~/.claude/scripts/heavy-job'))
GREEN_REUSE_S = 86400  # a green result blocks a local rerun of the same code for this long
STOP_GRACE_S = 10
EXEC_WINDOW_TICKS = 10 * os.sysconf('SC_CLK_TCK')  # a container exec starts within this of its `docker exec` client
CONTAINER_CGROUP_RE = re.compile(r'/docker-([0-9a-f]{12,})\.scope|/docker/([0-9a-f]{12,})|/libpod-([0-9a-f]{12,})')
GENERIC_WORDS = {'bash', 'sh', 'exec', 'sudo', 'env', 'docker', 'ddev', 'compose'}


def _toolkit_config(piece, defaults):
    """The piece's toolkit config, checked: a wrong value keeps the default and a broken file never raises."""
    try:
        lib = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), 'lib')
        if lib not in sys.path:
            sys.path.insert(0, lib)
        from toolkit_config import load_checked as checked
        return checked(piece, defaults)
    except Exception:
        return dict(defaults)


CONFIG = _toolkit_config('cloud-tests', {'excluded_names': [], 'excluded_owners': [],
                                         'runner_session_title': 'Tests en la nube de {project}'})
# Projects whose code never leaves the machine through the cloud, by checkout or repository name and by GitHub owner.
EXCLUDED_NAMES = {n.strip().lower() for n in CONFIG['excluded_names']}
EXCLUDED_OWNERS = {o.strip().lower() for o in CONFIG['excluded_owners']}

# 2026-11-19: the account's 5-hour limit cut two projects' runners mid-suite, twice in one night. Past the deadline the
# runner was taken for mute, a fresh one was launched inside the limit and died at once, and the run expired: the
# supervisor ran the suite locally and four stopped cloud sessions were left in the sidebar. The result of that expired
# run reached the results branch an hour after the reset: a cut cloud session can carry on by itself when usage comes
# back (another one, launched inside the limit, never did, and a follow-up sent to it the next day was not acted on).
# Now the account's usage limit is a state of its own. While it lasts nothing
# is launched, sent or expired and no deadline runs; when it is over, a run that was in the cloud during it gets a whole
# new deadline counted from the end of the limit, so a session that resumes by itself is waited for. If it stays silent
# after that, it is a mute runner as before: a fresh runner and one more attempt.
LIMIT_CACHE_S = 120          # the account's usage is asked at most this often (shared by every project)
LIMIT_FRESH_429_S = 15 * 60  # a refused turn this recent wins over a usage answer that says «not limited»
LIMIT_LOOKBACK_S = 6 * 3600  # refused turns are looked for this far back when the usage endpoint does not answer
LIMIT_HISTORY_S = 48 * 3600  # limit windows kept in the ledger
LIMIT_RESUME_GRACE_MIN = 30  # a cut cloud session took ~26 min to start again after the reset (19-11 03:50 -> 04:16)
ACCOUNT_SWITCH = os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_ACCOUNT_SWITCH', os.path.expanduser('~/.claude/scripts/account-switch'))


def die(code, line):
    print(line)
    sys.exit(code)


def run(cmd, cwd=None, check=True, env=None, timeout=None):
    p = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=cwd, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True, env=env, timeout=timeout)
    if check and p.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError(f"{' '.join(cmd)}: {p.stderr.strip() or p.stdout.strip()}")
    return p


def git(args, cwd, check=True):
    return run(['git', *args], cwd=cwd, check=check).stdout.strip()


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- project

class Project:
    def __init__(self, repo):
        self.dir = os.path.realpath(repo or os.getcwd())
        top = run(['git', 'rev-parse', '--show-toplevel'], cwd=self.dir, check=False)
        if top.returncode != 0:
            die(3, 'LOCAL not a git repository')
        self.top = top.stdout.strip()
        common = git(['rev-parse', '--path-format=absolute', '--git-common-dir'], self.top)
        self.common = os.path.realpath(common)
        self.checkout = os.path.dirname(self.common) if os.path.basename(self.common) == '.git' else self.top
        self.name = os.path.basename(self.checkout)
        self.key = self._key()
        self.origin = git(['remote', 'get-url', 'origin'], self.top, check=False)
        self.slug = github_slug(self.origin)

    def _key(self):
        lock = os.path.expanduser('~/.claude/scripts/supervisor-lock')
        if os.path.exists(lock) and not os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_OWN_KEY'):
            p = run([lock, 'project'], cwd=self.top, check=False)
            m = re.search(r'^key=(\S+)$', p.stdout, re.M)
            if p.returncode == 0 and m:
                return m.group(1)
        return f"{self.name}-{hashlib.sha1(self.common.encode()).hexdigest()[:8]}"


def github_slug(url):
    if os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_ALLOW_ANY_REMOTE') and url:
        return 'local/' + os.path.basename(url.rstrip('/')).removesuffix('.git')
    m = re.match(r'^(?:git@github(?:\.com|-[\w.-]+):|ssh://git@github\.com/|https://github\.com/)([\w.-]+)/([\w.-]+?)(?:\.git)?/?$',
                 url or '')
    return f'{m.group(1)}/{m.group(2)}' if m else None


def excluded(proj):
    names = {proj.name.lower(), (proj.slug or '').split('/')[-1].lower()}
    owner = (proj.slug or '/').split('/')[0].lower()
    return bool(names & EXCLUDED_NAMES) or owner in EXCLUDED_OWNERS


def claude_bin():
    return os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_CLAUDE') or shutil.which('claude')


def eligibility(proj, sha=None):
    if not proj.slug:
        return 'no GitHub remote: the cloud clones from GitHub'
    if excluded(proj):
        return 'excluded project: its code does not go to the cloud'
    if not claude_bin() or not shutil.which('script'):
        return 'claude CLI or script(1) missing'
    ref = sha or 'HEAD'
    if run(['git', 'cat-file', '-e', f'{ref}:{RECIPE}'], cwd=proj.top, check=False).returncode != 0:
        return f'no {RECIPE} committed at {ref[:12]}: the project has not prepared its cloud setup yet'
    return None


def load_recipe(proj, sha):
    try:
        return json.loads(git(['show', f'{sha}:{RECIPE}'], proj.top))
    except (RuntimeError, ValueError) as e:
        die(3, f'LOCAL unreadable {RECIPE} at {sha[:12]}: {e}')


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ledger

@contextlib.contextmanager
def ledger(proj):
    os.makedirs(STATE_DIR, exist_ok=True)
    path = os.path.join(STATE_DIR, f'{proj.key}.json')
    with open(path + '.lock', 'a+') as lk:
        fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        data = {'project': proj.key, 'repo': proj.slug, 'runner': None, 'runs': {}, 'results_seen': None}
        if os.path.exists(path):
            with open(path) as f:
                data.update(json.load(f))
        data['common'] = proj.common  # local-guard finds the ledger of a directory by its git common dir
        data['name'] = proj.name      # the runner title names the project; `sweep` reads it from here
        yield data
        tmp = path + '.tmp'
        with open(tmp, 'w') as f:
            json.dump(data, f, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)
        os.replace(tmp, path)


def run_key(tree, command):
    return f"{tree}:{hashlib.sha256(command.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]}"


def new_run_id():
    return time.strftime('%Y%m%d-%H%M%S') + '-' + secrets.token_hex(2)


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the runner

BRIEF = """Eres el corredor de las pruebas del proyecto {name} ({slug}) en una sesion de la nube. Lo ha puesto su
supervisora para que las suites no ocupen los huecos de la maquina local. Trabajas desatendido: nadie va a
contestar, asi que nunca preguntes ni esperes permiso; si algo falla, lo dices en el resultado.

Reglas:
- Solo corres tests. Nunca cambias codigo ni haces commit, merge, push o deploy en ninguna rama, aunque las reglas del
  repositorio lo permitan a las sesiones de la nube. La unica excepcion es publicar el fichero del resultado en la rama
  `{branch}`, como se explica abajo.
- Identidad: antes de ese commit, `git var GIT_AUTHOR_IDENT` tiene que ser la del desarrollador, la misma persona que
  firma `git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>' origin/HEAD`, y no Claude ni anthropic. Si no lo es, no hagas el commit y pon
  `"identity":"claude"` en la linea final.
- Preparacion: el arranque de la sesion (hook SessionStart del repositorio con CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE=true) deja el entorno.
  Si falta algo, ejecuta el `setup` de `{recipe}` del commit pedido (es idempotente). No instales nada mas.
- Cada peticion llega en una linea `CLOUD-TESTS-REQUEST {{json}}` con run, sha, tree, suite, command y timeout_min.
  Para cada una:
  1. `git fetch -q origin <sha>` (si no basta, `git fetch -q origin`), `git checkout -q --detach <sha>`, y comprueba que
     `git rev-parse HEAD^{{tree}}` es el tree pedido.
  2. Comprueba el kit: `sha256sum /tmp/cloud-tests-kit.py` tiene que dar {kit_sha}. Si no existe o no coincide,
     escribelo con el texto exacto que va al final de este mensaje entre las lineas `{kit_begin}` y `{kit_end}`
     (sin esas dos lineas), con `cat > /tmp/cloud-tests-kit.py <<'CLOUD_TESTS_KIT_EOF'`, y vuelve a comprobarlo. Si
     sigue sin coincidir, continua igualmente y dilo en summary.
     Guarda la peticion (el JSON de la linea, sin el prefijo) en /tmp/<run>.request.json y, desde la raiz del
     checkout, lanza en una sola orden:
       nohup python3 /tmp/cloud-tests-kit.py run /tmp/<run>.request.json > /tmp/<run>.kit.out 2>&1 &
     El kit corre el comando una vez, en un solo proceso y con todo lo que necesita (no exportes nada tu: las variables
     no pasan de una orden tuya a otra), con la salida en /tmp/<run>.log; lo para a los timeout_min (exit 124) y deja
     /tmp/<run>.tests.tsv (una linea `resultado<TAB>id` por test) y /tmp/<run>.result.json. Espera a que exista
     /tmp/<run>.result.json mirando cada pocos minutos, sin pasar de timeout_min + 5 minutos. No corras el comando por
     tu cuenta ni lo repitas.
  3. Escribe el resultado en JSON: run, suite, sha, tree; exit, duration_s, cores, tests_file y tests_counts tal como
     los da /tmp/<run>.result.json; summary (una linea: tests, aserciones, fallos), failures (hasta 30 nombres de tests
     que fallaron: las lineas failed y error de /tmp/<run>.tests.tsv si existe, si no los del log), log_tail (las
     ultimas 120 lineas de /tmp/<run>.log) y finished_at (ISO 8601). Si tests_file es null, summary dice que no hay
     resultado por test. Si no hay /tmp/<run>.result.json al acabar el plazo o no pudiste correrlo, exit 97 y la
     causa en summary.
  4. Publicalo sin tocar el checkout de trabajo:
       R=$(mktemp -d); git clone -q --no-checkout . "$R"; git -C "$R" remote set-url origin "$(git remote get-url origin)"
       cd "$R"; if git ls-remote --exit-code origin refs/heads/{branch} >/dev/null; then
         git fetch -q origin {branch} && git checkout -q -B {branch} FETCH_HEAD; else
         git checkout -q --orphan {branch} && git rm -rqf --cached --ignore-unmatch . ; fi
       mkdir -p runs; (escribe runs/<run>.json); git add runs/<run>.json
       if [ -f /tmp/<run>.tests.tsv ]; then cp /tmp/<run>.tests.tsv runs/; git add runs/<run>.tests.tsv; fi
       git commit -qm "cloud-tests: <run> [skip ci]" && git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/{branch}
     El fichero de tests va en el mismo commit que el JSON.
     Si el push se rechaza por una carrera: fetch, `git rebase FETCH_HEAD` y reintenta, hasta 5 veces.
  5. Termina el turno con una sola linea final: `CLOUD-TESTS-RESULT {{el mismo JSON sin log_tail}}`.
- Entre peticiones no hagas nada.
"""


def kit_text():
    """The runner kit, ending in exactly one newline (what the runner's heredoc writes back)."""
    with open(KIT_FILE, encoding='utf-8') as f:
        return f.read().rstrip('\n') + '\n'


def kit_sha():
    try:
        return hashlib.sha256(kit_text().encode()).hexdigest()
    except OSError:
        return None


def brief_for(proj):
    kit = kit_text()
    text = BRIEF.format(name=proj.name, slug=proj.slug or '?', branch=RESULTS_BRANCH, recipe=RECIPE,
                        kit_sha=hashlib.sha256(kit.encode()).hexdigest(), kit_begin=KIT_BEGIN, kit_end=KIT_END)
    return text + '\n' + KIT_BEGIN + '\n' + kit + KIT_END + '\n'


def request_line(entry):
    payload = {k: entry[k] for k in ('run', 'sha', 'tree', 'suite', 'command', 'timeout_min')}
    if entry.get('junit'):
        payload['junit'] = entry['junit']  # the suite writes its own JUnit file, relative to the checkout
    return 'CLOUD-TESTS-REQUEST ' + json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False)


def strip_ansi(text):
    text = re.sub(r'\x1b\[[0-9;?]*[ -/]*[@-~]', '', text)
    text = re.sub(r'\x1b[()][A-Z0-9]|\x1b[>=]', '', text)
    return text.replace('\r', '\n')


def via_tty(proj, argv, timeout):
    """The CLI refuses --cloud without a terminal, so it runs under script(1)."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix='cloud-tests-') as tmp:
        args_file = os.path.join(tmp, 'argv.json')
        with open(args_file, 'w') as f:
            json.dump(argv, f)
        inner = ('python3 -c ' + shlex.quote('import json,os,sys; a=json.load(open(sys.argv[1])); os.execvp(a[0], a)')
                 + ' ' + shlex.quote(args_file))
        log = os.path.join(tmp, 'tty.log')
        env = dict(os.environ, TERM='xterm-256color', COLUMNS='200', LINES='50')
        try:
            subprocess.run(['script', '-qfec', inner, log], cwd=proj.top, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                           stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, env=env, timeout=timeout)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            pass
        try:
            with open(log, errors='replace') as f:
                return strip_ansi(f.read())
        except FileNotFoundError:
            return ''


def launch_runner(proj, first_request):
    text = brief_for(proj) + '\nPrimera peticion:\n' + first_request
    out = via_tty(proj, [claude_bin(), '--cloud', text], timeout=150)
    m = re.search(r'\b(session_[A-Za-z0-9]+)\b', out)
    if not m or 'Created cloud session' not in out:
        tail = ' | '.join(l.strip() for l in out.splitlines() if l.strip() and not l.startswith('Script '))[-300:]
        return None, tail
    return m.group(1), None


def send_followup(proj, session, line):
    out = via_tty(proj, [claude_bin(), '-p', line, '--cloud', session], timeout=90)
    return 'Sent to cloud session' in out, out


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the account's usage limit

def _account_switch():
    import importlib.machinery
    import importlib.util
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader('account_switch_for_cloud_tests', ACCOUNT_SWITCH)
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


def _limit_from_account(now):
    """{until, what, source} while the account the CLI launches cloud sessions with is out of usage, else None.
    The usage endpoint (the CLI's own account) decides; a desktop turn refused with usage_limit_reached in the last
    LIMIT_FRESH_429_S still counts when it says «not limited» (it can read 99 % while turns are already refused), and
    the refused turns of the last LIMIT_LOOKBACK_S decide when it does not answer. Any failure means «not limited»:
    the old behaviour, never a hold on a guess."""
    try:
        acct = _account_switch()
    except (Exception, SystemExit):  # absent, or a copy that exits while loading: never take the account for limited
        return None
    try:
        data = acct.usage()
    except Exception:
        data = None
    if isinstance(data, dict):
        try:
            lim = acct.usage_limit(data)
        except Exception:
            lim = None
        if lim:
            return {'until': lim['until'], 'what': lim['what'], 'source': 'usage'}
        lookback = LIMIT_FRESH_429_S
    else:
        lookback = LIMIT_LOOKBACK_S
    try:
        lim = acct.transcript_limit(now - lookback)
    except Exception:
        lim = None
    return {'until': lim['until'], 'what': lim['what'], 'source': 'refused-turns'} if lim else None


def account_limit(now):
    """The account's usage limit now, cached LIMIT_CACHE_S in STATE_DIR/account-limit.json. $CLOUD_TESTS_LIMIT
    overrides it (tests): 'none', or the epoch the limit resets at."""
    forced = os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_LIMIT', '').strip()
    if forced:
        if forced == 'none':
            return None
        until = float(forced)
        return {'until': until, 'what': 'five_hour', 'source': 'env'} if until > now else None
    path = os.path.join(STATE_DIR, 'account-limit.json')
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            cached = json.load(f)
        if 0 <= now - cached.get('time', 0) < LIMIT_CACHE_S:
            lim = cached.get('limit')
            return lim if lim and lim.get('until', 0) > now else None
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        pass
    lim = _limit_from_account(now)
    try:
        os.makedirs(STATE_DIR, exist_ok=True)
        tmp = f'{path}.{os.getpid()}.tmp'
        with open(tmp, 'w') as f:
            json.dump({'time': now, 'limit': lim}, f)
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    except OSError:
        pass
    return lim


def note_limit(data, now):
    """Records the current limit (data['limit']) and its window (data['limits']: [{from, until}]); returns it."""
    lim = account_limit(now)
    windows = [w for w in data.get('limits') or [] if now - w.get('until', 0) < LIMIT_HISTORY_S]
    if lim:
        data['limit'] = lim
        last = windows[-1] if windows else None
        if last and last.get('until', 0) >= now - LIMIT_CACHE_S and last.get('from', now) <= now:
            last['until'] = max(last['until'], lim['until'])
        else:
            windows.append({'from': now, 'until': lim['until'], 'what': lim['what']})
    else:
        data.pop('limit', None)
        for w in windows:  # the limit ended earlier than announced (an account switch, extra usage): close the window
            if w.get('from', 0) <= now < w.get('until', 0):
                w['until'] = now
    if windows:
        data['limits'] = windows
    else:
        data.pop('limits', None)
    return lim


def cut_by_limit(data, e, now):
    """The end of the latest window of the account's limit, already over, that fell while the sent run `e` was in the
    cloud; 0 when none did."""
    start = e.get('dispatched')
    if start is None:
        return 0
    return max([w['until'] for w in data.get('limits') or []
                if w.get('from', 0) <= now and w.get('until', 0) > start and w.get('until', 0) <= now] or [0])


def last_limit_end(data, now):
    return max([w['until'] for w in data.get('limits') or [] if w.get('until', 0) <= now] or [0])


def hhmm(epoch):
    return time.strftime('%H:%M', time.localtime(epoch)) if epoch else '?'


def runner_usable(r, now):
    return bool(r) and not r.get('dead') and r.get('brief_version', 0) >= BRIEF_VERSION \
        and r.get('kit_sha') == kit_sha() \
        and r.get('runs', 0) < MAX_RUNS_PER_RUNNER and now - r.get('created', 0) < MAX_RUNNER_AGE_S


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- results

def fetch_results(proj, data):
    """Fetches the results branch when it moved; returns {run: result} for the files found."""
    p = run(['git', 'ls-remote', 'origin', f'refs/heads/{RESULTS_BRANCH}'], cwd=proj.top, check=False)
    if p.returncode != 0 or not p.stdout.strip():
        return {}
    remote_sha = p.stdout.split()[0]
    if data.get('results_seen') != remote_sha or \
            run(['git', 'rev-parse', '-q', '--verify', RESULTS_LOCAL_REF], cwd=proj.top, check=False).stdout.strip() != remote_sha:
        f = run(['git', 'fetch', '-q', 'origin', f'+refs/heads/{RESULTS_BRANCH}:{RESULTS_LOCAL_REF}'], cwd=proj.top, check=False)
        if f.returncode != 0:
            return {}
        data['results_seen'] = remote_sha
    found = {}
    names = run(['git', 'ls-tree', '--name-only', f'{RESULTS_LOCAL_REF}:runs'], cwd=proj.top, check=False).stdout.split()
    wanted = {rid for rid, e in data['runs'].items() if e.get('state') == 'sent'}
    for name in names:
        rid = name.removesuffix('.json')
        if rid in wanted:
            try:
                found[rid] = json.loads(git(['show', f'{RESULTS_LOCAL_REF}:runs/{name}'], proj.top))
            except (RuntimeError, ValueError):
                found[rid] = {'exit': 98, 'summary': 'unreadable result file'}
    return found


class LaunchFailed(Exception):
    pass


def queued_ids(data):
    """The queued runs, in dispatch order: oldest first (a re-queued run keeps its `created`, so it goes first)."""
    return sorted((rid for rid, e in data['runs'].items() if e.get('state') == 'queued'),
                  key=lambda rid: (data['runs'][rid].get('created', 0), rid))


def queued_since(e):
    return e.get('queued_at', e.get('created', 0))


def runner_busy(data):
    """True while a sent run belongs to the current runner's session: a dispatched one, or a legacy one (sent before
    the queue existed, no `dispatched`) until it settles. A dead runner is never busy: nobody waits for it."""
    r = data.get('runner')
    if not r or r.get('dead'):
        return False
    return any(e.get('state') == 'sent' and e.get('session') == r.get('session') for e in data['runs'].values())


def pending_runs(data):
    return any(e.get('state') in ('queued', 'sent') for e in data['runs'].values())


def dispatch(proj, data, now, fresh=None):
    """Sends the oldest queued run when the runner is free: a follow-up if the runner is usable, else a new runner.
    Returns the dispatched run id or None. A launch that fails expires the head run (`launch_failed`) and starts the
    launch backoff; for the run `fresh` (a request being made right now) it raises LaunchFailed instead and leaves the
    ledger untouched, so the caller keeps its contract (LAUNCH_FAILED, nothing recorded)."""
    queue = queued_ids(data)
    if not queue or runner_busy(data) or data.get('limit'):  # nothing leaves while the account is out of usage
        return None
    rid = queue[0]
    e = data['runs'][rid]
    line = request_line(e)
    r = data.get('runner')
    session, launched = None, False
    if runner_usable(r, now):
        ok, _ = send_followup(proj, r['session'], line)
        if ok:
            session = r['session']
        else:
            r['dead'] = True  # refused: the session is gone
    if not session:
        if data.get('launch_backoff_until', 0) > now:
            return None
        session, err = launch_runner(proj, line)
        if session:
            rename_session(session, runner_title(proj.name))  # a failure here never fails the launch
        if not session:
            if rid == fresh:
                raise LaunchFailed(err or 'no session id in the CLI output')
            e['state'] = 'expired'
            e['expired_reason'] = 'launch_failed'
            e['finished'] = now
            data['launch_backoff_until'] = now + LAUNCH_BACKOFF_S
            return None
        if r and r.get('session'):  # `sweep` archives it in the cloud once nobody needs it
            data['retired'] = (data.get('retired') or [])[-49:] + [
                {'session': r['session'], 'created': r.get('created'), 'retired': now}]
        data['runner'] = r = {'session': session, 'created': now, 'runs': 0, 'brief_version': BRIEF_VERSION,
                              'kit_sha': kit_sha()}
        data.pop('launch_backoff_until', None)
        launched = True
    r['runs'] = r.get('runs', 0) + 1
    r['last_used'] = now
    e['state'] = 'sent'
    e['session'] = session
    e['dispatched'] = now
    e['deadline'] = now + (e['timeout_min'] + (LAUNCH_OVERHEAD_MIN if launched else DISPATCH_OVERHEAD_MIN)) * 60
    return rid


def settle(proj, data, now, fresh=None):
    """Moves runs along: sent -> done / mismatch (result found) or, past the deadline, back to the queue once with a
    new runner (dispatched runs) or expired (legacy runs, or a second time); queued -> expired when it waited too long;
    then dispatches the queue head. Returns the runs that changed."""
    changed = []
    limited = note_limit(data, now)
    for rid, res in fetch_results(proj, data).items():
        e = data['runs'][rid]
        e['result'] = res
        e['state'] = 'done' if str(res.get('tree', e['tree'])) == e['tree'] else 'mismatch'
        e['finished'] = now
        changed.append(rid)
    if limited:  # out of usage: no deadline runs, nothing expires, nothing is sent; the queue just waits
        return changed
    queue_clock = last_limit_end(data, now)  # the time in the queue starts again when a limit ends
    for rid, e in data['runs'].items():
        cut_end = cut_by_limit(data, e, now) if e.get('state') == 'sent' else 0
        if cut_end and cut_end > e.get('limit_extended_to', 0):
            # The limit fell while it was in the cloud and no result came yet. The session may carry on by itself now
            # that there is usage again: a whole new deadline from the end of the limit, once per limit window.
            changed.append(rid)
            e['limit_cuts'] = e.get('limit_cuts', 0) + 1
            e['limit_extended_to'] = cut_end
            e['deadline'] = max(e.get('deadline', 0),
                                cut_end + (e['timeout_min'] + LAUNCH_OVERHEAD_MIN + LIMIT_RESUME_GRACE_MIN) * 60)
        elif e.get('state') == 'sent' and now > e.get('deadline', 0):
            changed.append(rid)
            if 'dispatched' not in e:  # legacy: sent under the old scheme
                e['state'] = 'expired'
                continue
            r = data.get('runner')
            if r and r.get('session') == e.get('session'):
                r['dead'] = True  # silent past its deadline: nobody waits for that runner any more
            if e.get('redispatched'):
                e['state'] = 'expired'
                e['expired_reason'] = 'deadline'
                e['finished'] = now
            else:
                e['redispatched'] = 1
                e['state'] = 'queued'
                e['queued_at'] = now
                for k in ('session', 'dispatched', 'deadline'):
                    e.pop(k, None)
        elif e.get('state') == 'queued' and now - max(queued_since(e), queue_clock) > QUEUE_MAX_S:
            e['state'] = 'expired'
            e['expired_reason'] = 'queue'
            e['finished'] = now
            changed.append(rid)
    if dispatch(proj, data, now, fresh):
        changed.append('dispatch')
    return changed


def held_note(data):
    """' held_by_limit_until=HH:MM' while the account is out of usage, else ''."""
    lim = (data or {}).get('limit')
    return f" held_by_limit_until={hhmm(lim.get('until'))}" if lim else ''


def describe(rid, e, now, data=None):
    st = e.get('state')
    if st in ('done', 'local'):
        r = e.get('result') or {}
        src = 'local' if st == 'local' else 'cloud'
        return (f"DONE {rid} exit={r.get('exit')} source={src} suite={e['suite']} sha={e['sha'][:12]} "
                f"duration_s={r.get('duration_s')} summary={json.dumps(r.get('summary', ''), ensure_ascii=False)}")
    held = held_note(data)
    if st == 'sent':
        return (f"PENDING {rid} suite={e['suite']} sha={e['sha'][:12]} age_min={int((now - e['created']) / 60)} "
                f"deadline_in_min={int((e['deadline'] - now) / 60)}{held}")
    if st == 'queued':
        pos = queued_ids(data).index(rid) + 1 if data is not None and rid in queued_ids(data) else '?'
        return (f"QUEUED {rid} suite={e['suite']} sha={e['sha'][:12]} position={pos} "
                f"age_min={int((now - e['created']) / 60)}{held}"
                + (f" limit_cuts={e['limit_cuts']}" if e.get('limit_cuts') else ''))
    if st == 'superseded':
        return f"SUPERSEDED {rid} by {e.get('superseded_by')} suite={e['suite']} sha={e['sha'][:12]}"
    return f"{st.upper()} {rid} suite={e['suite']} sha={e['sha'][:12]}" + \
        (f" reason={e['expired_reason']}" if e.get('expired_reason') else '')


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- redundant local runs

def norm_command(cmd):
    """'IS_DDEV_PROJECT=true XDEBUG_MODE=off make ci', 'env make ci', "bash -c 'make ci'" and ['make', 'ci'] all
    give 'make ci'."""
    try:
        argv = shlex.split(cmd) if isinstance(cmd, str) else [str(a) for a in cmd]
    except ValueError:
        return str(cmd).strip()
    while argv and (re.match(r'^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=', argv[0]) or argv[0] == 'env'):
        argv = argv[1:]
    if len(argv) == 3 and os.path.basename(argv[0]) in ('bash', 'sh') and argv[1] in ('-c', '-lc'):
        return norm_command(argv[2])
    return ' '.join(argv)


SHELLS = ('bash', 'sh', 'dash', 'zsh')
WRAPPERS = {'timeout': 1, 'nice': 0, 'ionice': 0, 'stdbuf': 0, 'time': 0, 'command': 0, 'exec': 0}
# What sessions put around a suite in the same shell line without changing what it tests.
SAFE_PROGS = {'echo', 'printf', 'test', '[', '[[', 'true', ':', 'cd', 'pwd', 'date', 'sleep', 'export', 'set', 'wc',
              'cat', 'head', 'tail', 'tee', 'grep', 'ls'}
SAFE_GIT = {'status', 'rev-parse', 'log', 'diff', 'show', 'branch', 'describe', 'fetch'}


def command_parts(cmd):
    """The simple commands of a command line (argv list or string), `bash -c` / `sh -c` unwrapped, each normalized
    (leading VAR=value, env, timeout N, nice... dropped). Splits on && || ; | and newlines."""
    if isinstance(cmd, str):
        try:
            argv = shlex.split(cmd)
        except ValueError:
            return [cmd.strip()] if cmd.strip() else []
    else:
        argv = [str(a) for a in cmd]
    while argv and (re.match(r'^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=', argv[0]) or argv[0] == 'env'):
        argv = argv[1:]
    while argv and os.path.basename(argv[0]) in WRAPPERS:
        skip = WRAPPERS[os.path.basename(argv[0])]
        argv = argv[1:]
        while argv and argv[0].startswith('-'):
            argv = argv[1:]
        argv = argv[skip:]
    if len(argv) >= 3 and os.path.basename(argv[0]) in SHELLS and re.match(r'^-[a-z]*c$', argv[1]):
        parts = []
        for piece in re.split(r'&&|\|\||;|\n|\|', argv[2]):
            parts.extend(command_parts(piece))
        return parts
    words, i = [], 0
    while i < len(argv):  # redirections (2>&1, > log, >>log, < in) do not change what runs
        w = argv[i]
        if w in ('>', '>>', '<', '2>', '2>>', '&>', '&>>'):
            i += 2
            continue
        if not re.match(r'^(\d*>>?|&>>?|<)\S+$|^\d*>&\d+$', w):
            words.append(w)
        i += 1
    return [' '.join(words)] if words else []


def safe_part(part):
    words = part.split()
    if not words:
        return True
    prog = os.path.basename(words[0].lstrip('({'))
    if prog == 'git':
        return len(words) > 1 and words[1] in SAFE_GIT
    return prog in SAFE_PROGS or prog in ('', ')', '}')


def same_suite(cmd, matches):
    """True when `cmd` runs one of `matches` (normalized suite commands) and nothing else but harmless commands. A line
    that also deploys or publishes is never taken for a redundant test run."""
    parts = command_parts(cmd)
    if not any(p in matches for p in parts):
        return False
    return all(safe_part(p) for p in parts if p not in matches)


def local_match(suite):
    """The local command lines that are the same suite: its command, `local_commands` and `equivalent_to`."""
    out = {norm_command(suite.get('command', ''))}
    out.update(norm_command(c) for c in suite.get('local_commands') or [])
    if suite.get('equivalent_to'):
        out.add(norm_command(re.sub(r'\s*\(.*$', '', suite['equivalent_to'])))
    out.discard('')
    return sorted(out)


def common_dir(cwd):
    p = run(['git', 'rev-parse', '--path-format=absolute', '--git-common-dir'], cwd=cwd, check=False)
    return os.path.realpath(p.stdout.strip()) if p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.strip() else None


def worktree_tree(cwd):
    """The tree a test run in `cwd` sees: HEAD plus uncommitted and untracked (not ignored) files. A copy of the index
    is used, so the checkout's own index is never touched."""
    top = git(['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel'], cwd)
    index = git(['rev-parse', '--path-format=absolute', '--git-path', 'index'], top)
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix='cloud-tests-tree-') as d:
        tmp_index = os.path.join(d, 'index')
        if os.path.exists(index):
            shutil.copyfile(index, tmp_index)
        env = dict(os.environ, GIT_INDEX_FILE=tmp_index)
        run(['git', 'add', '-A'], cwd=top, env=env, timeout=120)
        return run(['git', 'write-tree'], cwd=top, env=env).stdout.strip()


def heavy_job_module():
    from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader
    import importlib.util
    loader = SourceFileLoader('heavy_job', HEAVY_JOB_BIN)
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader('heavy_job', loader)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def local_jobs(hj):
    """heavy-job's cpu jobs: running ones (a held slot) and queued ones (a live ticket), as heavy-job describes them."""
    d = hj.state_dir()
    jobs, seen = [], set()
    for i in range(hj.slot_count()):
        if not hj.slot_is_held(d, i):
            continue
        info = hj.read_info(d, i)
        if not info or info.get('mode') != 'run':
            continue
        wrapper = info.get('wrapper_pid') or info.get('pid')
        if wrapper in seen:
            continue
        seen.add(wrapper)
        jobs.append(dict(info, state='running', wrapper=wrapper))
    queued = [dict(item['info'], state='queued', wrapper=item['pid'], pid=None) for item in hj.read_queue(d, prune=False)]
    return queued + jobs  # the queued ones first: stopping a running copy frees a slot that a queued copy would take


def redundant_jobs(proj, runs, hj=None):
    """[(run id, job)] for each local heavy-job job that runs the same suite on the same code as one of `runs`."""
    hj = hj or heavy_job_module()
    out, trees = [], {}
    for job in local_jobs(hj):
        cands = [(rid, e) for rid, e in runs
                 if same_suite(job.get('argv') or [], e.get('local_match') or [norm_command(e.get('command', ''))])]
        cwd = job.get('cwd') or ''
        if not cands or not os.path.isdir(cwd) or common_dir(cwd) != proj.common:
            continue
        if cwd not in trees:
            try:
                trees[cwd] = worktree_tree(cwd)
            except (RuntimeError, OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
                trees[cwd] = None
        for rid, e in cands:
            if trees[cwd] == e['tree']:
                out.append((rid, job))
                break
    return out


def processes():
    """pid -> {'ppid', 'start' (clock ticks since boot), 'uid', 'argv', 'container'} for every process we can read."""
    procs = {}
    for name in os.listdir('/proc'):
        if not name.isdigit():
            continue
        pid = int(name)
        try:
            with open(f'/proc/{pid}/stat') as f:
                raw = f.read()
            rest = raw[raw.rindex(')') + 2:].split()
            with open(f'/proc/{pid}/cmdline', 'rb') as f:
                argv = [a.decode(errors='replace') for a in f.read().split(b'\0') if a]
            with open(f'/proc/{pid}/cgroup') as f:
                cgroup = f.read()
            uid = os.stat(f'/proc/{pid}').st_uid
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        m = CONTAINER_CGROUP_RE.search(cgroup)
        procs[pid] = {'ppid': int(rest[1]), 'start': int(rest[19]), 'uid': uid, 'argv': argv, 'state': rest[0],
                      'container': next((g for g in m.groups() if g), None) if m else None}
    return procs


def subtree(root, procs):
    children = {}
    for pid, p in procs.items():
        children.setdefault(p['ppid'], []).append(pid)
    out, todo = [], [root]
    while todo:
        pid = todo.pop()
        if pid in procs and pid not in out:
            out.append(pid)
            todo.extend(children.get(pid, []))
    return out


def exec_client(argv):
    """True for `docker exec ...`, `docker compose exec ...`, `docker-compose exec ...` and `ddev exec ...`."""
    if not argv:
        return False
    prog = os.path.basename(argv[0])
    return prog in ('docker', 'docker-compose', 'ddev') and 'exec' in argv[1:4]


DOCKER_EXEC_VALUE_OPTS = {'-e', '--env', '--env-file', '-u', '--user', '-w', '--workdir', '--detach-keys', '--index'}


def exec_target(pid, procs):
    """The full id of the container a `docker exec` / `docker compose exec` / `ddev exec` client runs in, resolved with
    the client's own directory and environment (DOCKER_CONTEXT, COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME...), or None."""
    argv = procs[pid]['argv']
    try:
        cwd = os.readlink(f'/proc/{pid}/cwd')
        with open(f'/proc/{pid}/environ', 'rb') as f:
            env = dict(kv.split('=', 1) for kv in f.read().decode(errors='replace').split('\0') if '=' in kv)
    except OSError:
        return None
    env.setdefault('PATH', os.environ.get('PATH', ''))
    prog = os.path.basename(argv[0])
    rest = argv[argv.index('exec') + 1:]
    positional, i = None, 0
    while i < len(rest):
        w = rest[i]
        if w in DOCKER_EXEC_VALUE_OPTS or w in ('-s', '--service', '-d', '--dir') and prog == 'ddev':
            if prog == 'ddev' and w in ('-s', '--service') and i + 1 < len(rest):
                positional = rest[i + 1]
            i += 2
            continue
        if w.startswith('-'):
            if prog == 'ddev' and w.startswith('--service='):
                positional = w.split('=', 1)[1]
            i += 1
            continue
        if prog != 'ddev':
            positional = w
        break
    if prog == 'ddev':
        d = cwd
        while d != '/' and not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, '.ddev', 'config.yaml')):
            d = os.path.dirname(d)
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(d, '.ddev', 'config.yaml')) as f:
                m = re.search(r'^name:\s*["\']?([\w.-]+)', f.read(), re.M)
        except OSError:
            return None
        name = f"ddev-{m.group(1) if m else os.path.basename(d)}-{positional or 'web'}"
    elif 'compose' in argv[1:3] or prog == 'docker-compose':
        if not positional:
            return None
        cmd = ['docker', 'compose', 'ps', '-q', positional] if prog == 'docker' else ['docker-compose', 'ps', '-q', positional]
        try:
            name = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=cwd, env=env, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20).stdout.split()[0]
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, IndexError):
            return None
    else:
        name = positional
    if not name:
        return None
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(['docker', 'inspect', '-f', '{{.Id}}', name], env=env, capture_output=True, text=True,
                             timeout=20)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    return out.stdout.strip() if out.returncode == 0 and re.match(r'^[0-9a-f]{64}$', out.stdout.strip()) else None


def container_execs(clients, procs):
    """The exec processes a `docker exec` / `ddev exec` client started inside its container. They outlive their
    client, so stopping the client is not enough. Matched by the container the client targets (its id against the
    process's cgroup), our uid, start time (within EXEC_WINDOW_TICKS after the client) and a word of the client's
    command in the container's command line. Returns (pids, clients whose container could not be resolved)."""
    roots = [pid for pid, p in procs.items() if p['container'] and not procs.get(p['ppid'], {}).get('container')
             and p['uid'] == os.getuid()]
    found, unresolved = [], []
    for c in clients:
        cp = procs[c]
        target = exec_target(c, procs)
        if not target:
            unresolved.append(c)
            continue
        words = {w for w in cp['argv'][cp['argv'].index('exec') + 1:] if len(w) >= 4 and not w.startswith('-')}
        words |= {os.path.basename(w) for w in words}
        words -= GENERIC_WORDS
        for r in roots:
            if procs[r]['container'] != target or not 0 <= procs[r]['start'] - cp['start'] <= EXEC_WINDOW_TICKS:
                continue
            tree = subtree(r, procs)
            text = ' '.join(' '.join(procs[p]['argv']) for p in tree)
            if any(w in text for w in words):
                found.extend(tree)
    return found, unresolved


def alive(pid):
    try:
        with open(f'/proc/{pid}/stat') as f:
            raw = f.read()
        return raw[raw.rindex(')') + 2:].split()[0] != 'Z'
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return False


def stop_job(hj, rid, e, job):
    """Stop one redundant local job: leave the note for its wrapper, SIGTERM its process tree (and its container
    execs), SIGKILL what is still there after STOP_GRACE_S. Returns a one-line description."""
    wrapper = job['wrapper']
    note = (f"esa suite corre en la nube para este mismo código (run {rid}, suite {e['suite']}, commit {e['sha'][:12]}): "
            f"el resultado llega con `~/.claude/scripts/cloud-tests wait {rid}`. No la relances aquí.")
    stopped_dir = os.path.join(hj.state_dir(), getattr(hj, 'CLOUD_STOPPED_DIR', 'cloud-stopped'))
    os.makedirs(stopped_dir, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(stopped_dir, f'{wrapper}.txt'), 'w') as f:
        f.write(note + '\n')
    procs = processes()
    host = subtree(wrapper, procs)
    inside, unresolved = container_execs([p for p in host if exec_client(procs[p]['argv'])], procs)
    targets = [p for p in host if p != wrapper] + inside
    for sig_round, sig in enumerate((signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGKILL)):
        for pid in ([wrapper] if sig_round == 0 else []) + targets:
            try:
                os.kill(pid, sig)
            except OSError:
                pass
        end = time.time() + STOP_GRACE_S
        while time.time() < end and any(alive(p) for p in targets):
            time.sleep(0.2)
        targets = [p for p in targets if alive(p)]
        if not targets:
            break
    end = time.time() + STOP_GRACE_S
    while time.time() < end and alive(wrapper):  # it prints the note and leaves once its child is gone
        time.sleep(0.2)
    if alive(wrapper):
        try:
            os.kill(wrapper, signal.SIGKILL)
        except OSError:
            pass
    left = [p for p in targets if alive(p)]
    return (f"STOPPED {job['state']} run={rid} wrapper={wrapper} label={json.dumps(job.get('label') or '', ensure_ascii=False)} "
            f"cwd={job.get('cwd')} argv={json.dumps(' '.join(job.get('argv') or []), ensure_ascii=False)} "
            f"container_procs={len(inside)}" + (f" still_alive={left}" if left else '')
            + (f" container_unresolved={unresolved}" if unresolved else ''))


def stop_redundant(proj, rids=None):
    """Stop the local heavy-job jobs that duplicate in-flight (or green) runs of this project. Prints and records."""
    now = time.time()
    with ledger(proj) as data:
        runs = [(rid, dict(e)) for rid, e in data['runs'].items() if (rids is None or rid in rids) and blocking(e, now)]
    if not runs:
        return []
    try:
        hj = heavy_job_module()
        jobs = redundant_jobs(proj, runs, hj)
    except Exception as err:  # never let the cleanup break a request or a wait
        print(f'WARN no pude mirar los trabajos locales de heavy-job: {err}')
        return []
    lines = []
    for rid, job in jobs:
        try:
            lines.append(stop_job(hj, rid, dict(runs)[rid], job))
        except Exception as err:
            lines.append(f"WARN no pude parar wrapper={job.get('wrapper')}: {err}")
    if lines:
        with ledger(proj) as data:
            for line in lines:
                m = re.search(r'run=(\S+)', line)
                if m and m.group(1) in data['runs']:
                    data['runs'][m.group(1)].setdefault('stopped_local', []).append({'at': now, 'what': line})
        for line in lines:
            print(line)
    return lines


def blocking(e, now):
    """A run that makes the same local run redundant: in flight in the cloud, or green within GREEN_REUSE_S."""
    if e.get('state') == 'queued':
        return now - queued_since(e) <= QUEUE_MAX_S
    if e.get('state') == 'sent':
        return now <= e.get('deadline', 0)
    if e.get('state') in ('done', 'local'):
        return (e.get('result') or {}).get('exit') == 0 and now - e.get('finished', e.get('created', 0)) <= GREEN_REUSE_S
    return False


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- commands

def resolve_ref(proj, ref):
    branch = ref or git(['symbolic-ref', '--short', '-q', 'HEAD'], proj.top, check=False)
    if not branch:
        die(4, 'NOT_PUSHED detached HEAD: pass --ref <pushed branch>')
    local = git(['rev-parse', '--verify', '-q', f'refs/heads/{branch}^{{commit}}'], proj.top, check=False)
    remote = run(['git', 'ls-remote', 'origin', f'refs/heads/{branch}'], cwd=proj.top, check=False).stdout.split()
    remote_sha = remote[0] if remote else ''
    if not local:
        die(4, f'NOT_PUSHED {branch}: no such local branch')
    if local != remote_sha:
        die(4, f'NOT_PUSHED {branch} local={local[:12]} origin={remote_sha[:12] or "-"}: push it first (project rules), then retry')
    return branch, local, git(['rev-parse', f'{local}^{{tree}}'], proj.top)


def cmd_check(args):
    proj = Project(args.repo)
    why = eligibility(proj)
    if why:
        die(3, f'LOCAL {why}')
    print(f'ELIGIBLE {proj.slug} key={proj.key}')


def find_existing(data, key, now):
    """(run id, line) of the run that makes a new request with this key redundant, or None: a finished one is REUSEd,
    one queued or in flight is WAITed for."""
    for rid, e in sorted(data['runs'].items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]['created'], reverse=True):
        if e['key'] != key:
            continue
        if e['state'] in ('done', 'local'):
            if (e.get('result') or {}).get('exit') in RETRYABLE_EXITS:
                continue
            return rid, 'REUSE ' + describe(rid, e, now, data)[5:]
        if e['state'] == 'sent':
            return rid, f"WAIT {rid} session={e.get('session')} " + describe(rid, e, now, data)[8 + len(rid):]
        if e['state'] == 'queued':
            return rid, f'WAIT {rid} queued ' + describe(rid, e, now, data)[8 + len(rid):]
    return None


def run_preflight(proj, recipe, name, suite, tree, skip):
    """The recipe's check-only commands (a suite's own `preflight` overrides the top-level one), run locally under
    heavy-job before the run is queued. Skipped, saying so, when the checkout is not exactly the pushed tree."""
    cmds = suite.get('preflight', recipe.get('preflight')) or []
    if isinstance(cmds, str):
        cmds = [cmds]
    if not cmds:
        return
    if skip:
        print(f'PREFLIGHT_SKIPPED {name} (--skip-preflight)')
        return
    try:
        same = worktree_tree(proj.top) == tree
    except (RuntimeError, OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        same = False
    if not same:
        print(f'PREFLIGHT_SKIPPED {name} (the checkout is not the pushed commit)')
        return
    if not os.access(HEAVY_JOB_BIN, os.X_OK):
        print(f'PREFLIGHT_SKIPPED {name} (heavy-job is not installed)')
        return
    for cmd in cmds:
        argv = [HEAVY_JOB_BIN, 'run', '--kind', 'typecheck', '--label', f'cloud-tests preflight {name}', '--',
                'bash', '-c', cmd]
        proc = subprocess.Popen(argv, cwd=proj.top, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True,
                                start_new_session=True)
        try:
            out = proc.communicate(timeout=PREFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_S)[0]
            code = proc.returncode
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            try:
                os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGTERM)
            except OSError:
                pass
            out = (proc.communicate()[0] or '') + f'\n(preflight timed out after {PREFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_S // 60} min)'
            code = 124
        if code != 0:
            print(f'PREFLIGHT_FAILED {name} exit={code} command={cmd}')
            print('\n'.join((out or '').rstrip().splitlines()[-40:]))
            sys.exit(6)


def ensure_pump(proj):
    """Spawns the detached pump (one per project, it takes a flock) so the queue moves with nobody waiting."""
    if os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_NO_PUMP') == '1':
        return
    try:
        log = open(os.path.join(STATE_DIR, f'{proj.key}.pump.log'), 'a')
        subprocess.Popen([os.path.realpath(__file__), '--repo', proj.top, 'pump'], start_new_session=True,
                         stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=log, stderr=log, cwd=proj.top)
    except OSError as e:
        print(f'WARN no pude lanzar el pump: {e}')


def cmd_request(args):
    proj = Project(args.repo)
    branch, sha, tree = resolve_ref(proj, args.ref)
    why = eligibility(proj, sha)
    if why:
        die(3, f'LOCAL {why}')
    recipe = load_recipe(proj, sha)
    suite = (recipe.get('suites') or {}).get(args.suite)
    if not suite or not suite.get('command'):
        die(3, f'LOCAL suite {args.suite!r} is not in {RECIPE} (cloud suites: {", ".join(recipe.get("suites", {})) or "none"})')
    command = suite['command']
    timeout_min = int(args.deadline_min or suite.get('timeout_min') or DEFAULT_DEADLINE_MIN)
    junit = suite.get('junit')
    if junit and (not isinstance(junit, str) or os.path.isabs(junit) or '..' in junit.split('/')):
        die(3, f'LOCAL suite {args.suite!r}: junit must be a path inside the checkout, got {junit!r}')
    key = run_key(tree, command)
    now = time.time()
    with ledger(proj) as data:
        settle(proj, data, now)
        found = find_existing(data, key, now)
        pending = pending_runs(data)
    if found:
        print(found[1])
        if pending:
            ensure_pump(proj)
        stop_redundant(proj, {found[0]})  # only a queued, in-flight or green run stops anything (`blocking`)
        return
    run_preflight(proj, recipe, args.suite, suite, tree, args.skip_preflight)  # outside the lock: it can take minutes
    now = time.time()
    lines = []
    with ledger(proj) as data:
        settle(proj, data, now)
        found = find_existing(data, key, now)  # another session may have asked for the same code meanwhile
        if not found:
            rid = new_run_id()
            for old in [r for r, e in data['runs'].items() if e.get('state') == 'queued' and e.get('suite') == args.suite
                        and e.get('ref') == branch and e['key'] != key]:  # newer code on the same branch
                data['runs'][old].update(state='superseded', superseded_by=rid, finished=now)
                lines.append(f'SUPERSEDED {old} -> {rid}')
            entry = {'run': rid, 'key': key, 'suite': args.suite, 'command': command, 'ref': branch, 'sha': sha,
                     'tree': tree, 'timeout_min': timeout_min, 'requester': args.requester or os.environ.get('CLAUDE_SESSION_ID', ''),
                     'created': now, 'queued_at': now, 'state': 'queued', 'local_match': local_match(suite)}
            if junit:
                entry['junit'] = junit
            data['runs'][rid] = entry
            try:
                dispatch(proj, data, now, fresh=rid)
            except LaunchFailed as err:
                die(5, f'LAUNCH_FAILED {err}: run it locally with heavy-job')
            if entry['state'] == 'sent':
                lines.append(f"SENT {rid} session={entry['session']} suite={args.suite} sha={sha[:12]} tree={tree[:12]} "
                             f"deadline_min={round((entry['deadline'] - entry['dispatched']) / 60)}")
            else:
                lines.append(f"QUEUED {rid} position={queued_ids(data).index(rid) + 1} suite={args.suite} "
                             f"sha={sha[:12]} tree={tree[:12]}{held_note(data)}")
        pending = pending_runs(data)
    if found:
        lines.append(found[1])
        rid = found[0]
    for line in lines:
        print(line)
    sys.stdout.flush()
    if pending:
        ensure_pump(proj)
    stop_redundant(proj, {rid})


def cmd_poll(args):
    proj = Project(args.repo)
    now = time.time()
    with ledger(proj) as data:
        settle(proj, data, now)
        for rid, e in sorted(data['runs'].items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]['created']):
            if now - e['created'] < 86400 or e.get('state') in ('sent', 'queued'):
                print(describe(rid, e, now, data))


def cmd_pump(args):
    """Keeps settling (and so dispatching) until nothing is queued or sent. One per project: it holds a flock."""
    proj = Project(args.repo)
    os.makedirs(STATE_DIR, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(STATE_DIR, f'{proj.key}.pump.lock'), 'a+') as lk:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except OSError:
            sys.exit(0)
        lk.seek(0)
        lk.truncate()
        lk.write(str(os.getpid()))
        lk.flush()
        interval = int(os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_PUMP_INTERVAL', 60))
        end = time.time() + PUMP_MAX_S
        failures = 0
        while time.time() < end:
            if not os.path.isdir(proj.top):  # the worktree it was started from is gone: let the next request respawn it
                print(f'pump stops: {proj.top} no longer exists')
                return
            try:
                with ledger(proj) as data:
                    settle(proj, data, time.time())
                    pending = pending_runs(data)
                    lim = data.get('limit')
                if lim and pending:  # a long limit (the weekly one) must not outlast the pump: it stays until after it
                    end = max(end, lim['until'] + 3600)
                failures = 0
            except Exception as err:  # a bad tick (git, network) must not kill the pump...
                failures += 1
                print(f'WARN pump tick failed ({failures}): {err}')
                if failures >= 5:  # ...but a pump that never works must not hold the lock for hours
                    return
                pending = True
            if not pending:
                return
            time.sleep(interval)


def cmd_wait(args):
    proj = Project(args.repo)
    end = time.time() + args.timeout
    targets = list(args.runs)
    announced = set()
    while True:
        now = time.time()
        with ledger(proj) as data:
            settle(proj, data, now)
            missing = [r for r in targets if r not in data['runs']]
            if missing:
                die(3, f'UNKNOWN {" ".join(missing)}')
            for i, r in enumerate(targets):  # a superseded run is waited for through its successor
                while data['runs'][r].get('state') == 'superseded' and data['runs'][r].get('superseded_by') in data['runs']:
                    nxt = data['runs'][r]['superseded_by']
                    if r not in announced:
                        announced.add(r)
                        print(f'SUPERSEDED {r} -> {nxt}')
                    r = nxt
                targets[i] = r
            targets = list(dict.fromkeys(targets))
            states = {r: data['runs'][r]['state'] for r in targets}
        stop_redundant(proj, set(targets))  # a local copy started meanwhile (outside heavy-job's guard window)
        if all(s not in ('sent', 'queued') for s in states.values()):
            with ledger(proj) as data:
                for r in targets:
                    print(describe(r, data['runs'][r], now, data))
            sys.exit(5 if any(s in ('expired', 'mismatch', 'superseded') for s in states.values()) else 0)
        if now >= end:
            print('TIMEOUT ' + ' '.join(targets))
            sys.exit(75)
        time.sleep(min(args.interval, max(1, end - now)))


def cmd_local_guard(args):
    """For heavy-job: exit 3 with the reason when running ARGV in CWD would repeat a cloud run (in flight, or green
    within GREEN_REUSE_S) of the same suite on the same code; exit 0 otherwise, and on any doubt."""
    try:
        names = [n for n in os.listdir(STATE_DIR) if n.endswith('.json')]
    except OSError:
        sys.exit(0)
    cwd = os.path.realpath(args.cwd or os.getcwd())
    common = common_dir(cwd) if names and args.argv else None
    if not common:
        sys.exit(0)
    now = time.time()
    for name in names:
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(STATE_DIR, name)) as f:
                data = json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        if data.get('common') != common:
            continue
        cands = sorted(((rid, e) for rid, e in (data.get('runs') or {}).items() if blocking(e, now)
                        and same_suite(args.argv, e.get('local_match') or [norm_command(e.get('command', ''))])),
                       key=lambda kv: kv[1].get('created', 0), reverse=True)
        if not cands:
            continue
        try:
            tree = worktree_tree(cwd)
        except (RuntimeError, OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            sys.exit(0)
        for rid, e in cands:
            if e.get('tree') != tree:
                continue
            if e['state'] in ('sent', 'queued'):
                print(f"esa suite ya corre en la nube para este mismo código (run {rid}, suite {e['suite']}, commit "
                      f"{e['sha'][:12]}). Espera su resultado con `~/.claude/scripts/cloud-tests wait {rid}` en segundo "
                      f"plano, sin ocupar un hueco aquí. [CLOUD_RUNNING {rid}]")
            else:
                src = 'en local' if e['state'] == 'local' else 'en la nube'
                print(f"esa suite ya pasó {src} para este mismo código (run {rid}, suite {e['suite']}, exit 0). Usa ese "
                      f"resultado: `~/.claude/scripts/cloud-tests result {rid}`. [CLOUD_DONE {rid}]")
            sys.exit(3)
    sys.exit(0)


def cmd_stop_local(args):
    proj = Project(args.repo)
    if not stop_redundant(proj, set(args.runs) if args.runs else None):
        print('NONE no redundant local job')


def print_tests(proj, rid, pattern):
    """The per-test lines the runner published for `rid` (`runs/<rid>.tests.tsv` on the results branch), optionally
    filtered by a regex. Exit 3 when the run has none."""
    try:
        wanted = re.compile(pattern) if pattern else None
    except re.error as e:
        die(2, f'BAD_REGEX {pattern!r}: {e}')
    if not re.fullmatch(r'[\w.-]+', rid):
        die(3, f'UNKNOWN {rid}')
    f = run(['git', 'fetch', '-q', 'origin', f'+refs/heads/{RESULTS_BRANCH}:{RESULTS_LOCAL_REF}'], cwd=proj.top, check=False)
    have_ref = run(['git', 'rev-parse', '-q', '--verify', RESULTS_LOCAL_REF], cwd=proj.top, check=False).returncode == 0
    if f.returncode != 0 and not have_ref:
        die(3, f'NO_TESTS_FILE {rid}: the results branch {RESULTS_BRANCH} is not on origin')
    p = run(['git', 'show', f'{RESULTS_LOCAL_REF}:runs/{rid}.tests.tsv'], cwd=proj.top, check=False)
    if p.returncode != 0:
        die(3, f'NO_TESTS_FILE {rid}: the run published no per-test result (runs/{rid}.tests.tsv); '
               'see the result JSON for its summary')
    lines = p.stdout.splitlines()
    if wanted:
        lines = [l for l in lines if wanted.search(l)]
        if not lines:
            print(f'NONE no test line of {rid} matches {pattern!r}', file=sys.stderr)
    for line in lines:
        print(line)


def cmd_result(args):
    proj = Project(args.repo)
    if args.tests:
        return print_tests(proj, args.run, args.grep)
    if args.grep:
        die(2, '--grep needs --tests')
    with ledger(proj) as data:
        e = data['runs'].get(args.run)
        if not e:
            die(3, f'UNKNOWN {args.run}')
        print(json.dumps(e, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))


def cmd_record_local(args):
    proj = Project(args.repo)
    branch = args.ref or git(['symbolic-ref', '--short', '-q', 'HEAD'], proj.top, check=False) or 'HEAD'
    sha = git(['rev-parse', f'{branch}^{{commit}}'], proj.top)
    tree = git(['rev-parse', f'{sha}^{{tree}}'], proj.top)
    try:
        recipe = json.loads(git(['show', f'{sha}:{RECIPE}'], proj.top))
        command = recipe['suites'][args.suite]['command']
    except (RuntimeError, ValueError, KeyError):
        command = args.command or args.suite
    now = time.time()
    with ledger(proj) as data:
        rid = args.run or new_run_id()
        e = data['runs'].get(rid) or {'run': rid, 'suite': args.suite, 'command': command, 'ref': branch, 'sha': sha,
                                       'tree': tree, 'key': run_key(tree, command), 'created': now, 'timeout_min': 0,
                                       'deadline': now}
        e['state'] = 'local'
        e['result'] = {'exit': args.exit, 'summary': args.summary, 'source': 'local', 'finished_at': time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z')}
        data['runs'][rid] = e
        print(f'RECORDED {rid} exit={args.exit} source=local sha={e["sha"][:12]}')


def cmd_status(args):
    proj = Project(args.repo)
    now = time.time()
    with ledger(proj) as data:
        r = data.get('runner')
        print(f"project={proj.key} repo={proj.slug} eligible={'yes' if not eligibility(proj) else 'no: ' + eligibility(proj)}")
        if r:
            print(f"runner={r['session']} runs={r.get('runs', 0)}/{MAX_RUNS_PER_RUNNER} age_h={int((now - r['created']) / 3600)}"
                  f"{' DEAD' if r.get('dead') else ''} "
                  f"usable={'yes' if runner_usable(r, now) else 'no'} busy={'yes' if runner_busy(data) else 'no'}")
        else:
            print('runner=none')
        lim = note_limit(data, now)
        if lim:
            print(f"account_limit={lim['what']} until={hhmm(lim['until'])} source={lim['source']}: nothing is launched, "
                  f"sent or expired until then; the queue moves by itself when it ends")
        if data.get('launch_backoff_until', 0) > now:
            print(f"launch_backoff_min={int((data['launch_backoff_until'] - now) / 60) + 1}")
        print(f"queued={len(queued_ids(data))}")
        for rid, e in sorted(data['runs'].items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]['created'])[-15:]:
            print('  ' + describe(rid, e, now, data))
        for rid in queued_ids(data):  # a queued run older than the last 15 would otherwise not show
            if rid not in [r_ for r_, _ in sorted(data['runs'].items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]['created'])[-15:]]:
                print('  ' + describe(rid, data['runs'][rid], now, data))


def cmd_runner(args):
    proj = Project(args.repo)
    with ledger(proj) as data:
        if args.forget and data.get('runner'):
            data['runner']['dead'] = True
            print(f"FORGOTTEN {data['runner']['session']}")
        else:
            print(json.dumps(data.get('runner'), ensure_ascii=False))


def cmd_brief(args):
    print(brief_for(Project(args.repo)))


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- retired runners (sweep)
# 2026-11-21: the sidebar showed several stopped cloud test runners, some with a warning, taken for hung sessions that
# no supervisor attended. Each runner that was replaced (mute, used up, too old, cut by the account's limit) stayed
# active in the cloud for good: 24 of them on 2026-11-21, the oldest from 2026-11-12. Supervisors cannot see cloud sessions with their tools, so `sweep` (run by the supervisor-watchdog timer)
# archives them, with the same call the CLI uses (POST /v1/code/sessions/<id>/archive, reversible from the archive).

API_BASE = os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_API', 'https://api.anthropic.com')
API_FAKE = os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_API_FAKE')  # self-test: a JSON file {"sessions": [...]}
CREDENTIALS = os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_CREDENTIALS', os.path.expanduser('~/.claude/.credentials.json'))
SWEEP_GRACE_S = int(os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_SWEEP_GRACE_S', str(3 * 3600)))
RUNNER_ENV_KIND = 'anthropic_cloud'  # a real cloud session; never 'bridge' (the Remote Control mirror of a local one)


class ApiUnavailable(Exception):
    pass


def sid_key(session):
    """'session_01X…' (what the CLI prints) and 'cse_01X…' (what the sessions API lists) are the same session."""
    s = str(session or '')
    for prefix in ('session_', 'cse_'):
        if s.startswith(prefix):
            return s[len(prefix):]
    return s


def api_headers():
    """The CLI's own login, read at call time; never refreshed or written here (the CLI renews it when it runs)."""
    try:
        with open(CREDENTIALS) as f:
            oauth = json.load(f).get('claudeAiOauth') or {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        raise ApiUnavailable('no CLI login')
    token = oauth.get('accessToken')
    if not token or oauth.get('expiresAt', 0) / 1000 < time.time() + 60:
        raise ApiUnavailable('the CLI login has expired (the CLI renews it the next time it runs)')
    return {'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json',
            'anthropic-version': '2023-06-01', 'User-Agent': 'cloud-tests (claude-cli)'}


def api_call(method, path, body=None):
    """(HTTP status, JSON body). Network trouble raises ApiUnavailable; an HTTP error is returned, not raised."""
    if API_FAKE:
        with open(API_FAKE) as f:
            st = json.load(f)
        if method == 'GET':
            return 200, {'data': [x for x in st['sessions'] if x.get('status') == 'active'], 'next_cursor': None}
        if method == 'PUT':  # a rename: PUT /v1/code/sessions/<id> {"title": …}
            sid = path.rstrip('/').split('/')[-1]
            hit = [x for x in st['sessions'] if x['id'] == sid]
            for x in hit:
                x['title'] = (body or {}).get('title')
            st['renamed'] = st.get('renamed', []) + [[sid, (body or {}).get('title')]]
            with open(API_FAKE, 'w') as f:
                json.dump(st, f)
            return (200 if hit else 404), {}
        sid = path.rstrip('/').split('/')[-2]
        hit = [x for x in st['sessions'] if x['id'] == sid]
        for x in hit:
            x['status'] = 'archived'
        st['archived'] = st.get('archived', []) + [sid]
        with open(API_FAKE, 'w') as f:
            json.dump(st, f)
        return (200 if hit else 404), {}
    import urllib.error
    import urllib.request
    req = urllib.request.Request(API_BASE + path, headers=api_headers(), method=method,
                                 data=None if body is None else json.dumps(body).encode())
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20) as resp:
            raw = resp.read()
            return resp.status, json.loads(raw) if raw else {}
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as err:
        return err.code, {}
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, ValueError) as err:
        raise ApiUnavailable(f'network: {err}')


def active_cloud_sessions():
    import urllib.parse
    rows, cursor = [], None
    for _ in range(20):
        q = '/v1/code/sessions?limit=100&statuses=active' + (f'&cursor={urllib.parse.quote(cursor)}' if cursor else '')
        code, body = api_call('GET', q)
        if code != 200:
            raise ApiUnavailable(f'listing the cloud sessions: HTTP {code}')
        rows += body.get('data') or []
        cursor = body.get('next_cursor')
        if not cursor:
            break
    return rows


def iso_epoch(text):
    from datetime import datetime
    try:
        return datetime.fromisoformat(str(text).replace('Z', '+00:00')).timestamp()
    except ValueError:
        return 0


@contextlib.contextmanager
def ledger_by_key(key):
    """The ledger of a project by its key, under the same lock as `ledger`; written back only if it changed."""
    path = os.path.join(STATE_DIR, f'{key}.json')
    with open(path + '.lock', 'a+') as lk:
        fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        with open(path) as f:
            data = json.load(f)
        before = json.dumps(data, sort_keys=True)
        yield data
        if json.dumps(data, sort_keys=True) != before:
            tmp = path + '.tmp'
            with open(tmp, 'w') as f:
                json.dump(data, f, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)
            os.replace(tmp, path)


def ledger_keys():
    if not os.path.isdir(STATE_DIR):
        return []
    return sorted(n[:-5] for n in os.listdir(STATE_DIR) if n.endswith('.json') and n != 'account-limit.json')


def runner_title(name):
    """The title of the runners of the project called `name` (config `runner_session_title`)."""
    return CONFIG['runner_session_title'].replace('{project}', str(name))


def rename_session(session, title):
    """Sets the title of a cloud session with PUT /v1/code/sessions/<id> (the call the CLI makes itself; the id is the
    `cse_…` form the API lists, `session_…` is what the CLI prints). Returns the HTTP status, or None when the API cannot
    be reached. Never raises: a title is cosmetic and must not fail a launch or a sweep."""
    try:
        code, _ = api_call('PUT', f'/v1/code/sessions/cse_{sid_key(session)}', {'title': title})
        return code
    except Exception:
        return None


def rename_targets(data, sessions, now, archiving=()):
    """(session, expected title) for the active runners this ledger proves are its own whose title differs. The proof is
    the one `sweep_targets` asks for, minus the idle and busy rules (a working runner is renamed too). A ledger written
    before it recorded the project name takes it from the checkout of its git common dir, else renames nothing: the
    title is never guessed."""
    name = data.get('name')
    common = data.get('common') or ''
    if not name and os.path.basename(common) == '.git':   # a ledger from before it recorded the name: Project.name's rule
        name = os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(common))
    if not name or not isinstance(data.get('runs'), dict):
        return []
    want = runner_title(name)
    r = data.get('runner') or {}
    proven = {sid_key(x.get('session')) for x in data.get('retired') or []}
    proven |= {sid_key(e.get('session')) for e in data['runs'].values() if e.get('session')}
    proven.add(sid_key(r.get('session')))
    proven.discard('')
    skip = {sid_key(s.get('id')) for s in archiving}
    repo = (data.get('repo') or '').lower()
    out = []
    for s in sessions:
        k = sid_key(s.get('id'))
        if k not in proven or k in skip or s.get('title') == want:
            continue
        if s.get('environment_kind') != RUNNER_ENV_KIND or s.get('status') != 'active':
            continue
        urls = [str(x.get('url', '')).lower() for x in (s.get('config') or {}).get('sources') or [] if isinstance(x, dict)]
        if repo and any(urls) and not any(repo in u for u in urls):
            continue
        out.append((s, want))
    return out


def sweep_targets(data, sessions, now):
    """The cloud sessions this ledger proves are its runners and that nobody needs any more. A session qualifies only if
    its id is in the ledger (the runner, a retired one or a run's session), it is a real cloud session, still active,
    not working, quiet for SWEEP_GRACE_S (a runner cut by a limit may still publish its result: 2026-11-19), no sent run
    waits on it, and it is not the usable current runner (a current one that failed or is used up does go)."""
    r = data.get('runner') or {}
    proven = {sid_key(x.get('session')) for x in data.get('retired') or []}
    proven |= {sid_key(e.get('session')) for e in data['runs'].values() if e.get('session')}
    proven.add(sid_key(r.get('session')))
    proven.discard('')
    busy = {sid_key(e.get('session')) for e in data['runs'].values() if e.get('state') == 'sent'}
    current = sid_key(r.get('session'))
    repo = (data.get('repo') or '').lower()
    out = []
    for s in sessions:
        k = sid_key(s.get('id'))
        if k not in proven or k in busy:
            continue
        if s.get('environment_kind') != RUNNER_ENV_KIND or s.get('status') != 'active' \
                or s.get('worker_status') == 'running':
            continue
        if now - iso_epoch(s.get('last_event_at') or s.get('updated_at') or '') < SWEEP_GRACE_S:
            continue
        if k == current and runner_usable(r, now) and s.get('status_bucket') != 'failed':
            continue
        urls = [str(x.get('url', '')).lower() for x in (s.get('config') or {}).get('sources') or [] if isinstance(x, dict)]
        if repo and any(urls) and not any(repo in u for u in urls):
            continue  # paranoia: an id from this ledger on another repository is not ours to touch
        out.append(s)
    return out


def cmd_sweep(args):
    """Archives the project runners nobody needs (see sweep_targets) across every ledger. Never fails the caller."""
    now = time.time()
    try:
        sessions = active_cloud_sessions()
    except ApiUnavailable as err:
        print(f'SKIP {err}')
        return
    log = os.path.join(STATE_DIR, 'sweep.log')
    for key in ledger_keys():
        try:
            with ledger_by_key(key) as data:
                if not isinstance(data.get('runs'), dict):
                    continue
                targets = sweep_targets(data, sessions, now)
                r = data.get('runner') or {}
                if not args.dry_run and any(sid_key(s['id']) == sid_key(r.get('session')) for s in targets):
                    r['dead'] = True  # failed or used up: the next run launches a fresh runner
            done = []
            for s in targets:
                line = (f"{key} {s['id']} bucket={s.get('status_bucket')} last={str(s.get('last_event_at'))[:16]} "
                        f"title={json.dumps((s.get('title') or '')[:60], ensure_ascii=False)}")
                if args.dry_run:
                    print(f'WOULD_ARCHIVE {line}')
                    continue
                code, _ = api_call('POST', f"/v1/code/sessions/{s['id']}/archive", {})
                if code in (200, 404, 409):  # archived now, already gone, already archived
                    print(f'ARCHIVED {line}')
                    done.append(s['id'])
                    with open(log, 'a') as f:
                        f.write(f"{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z')} ARCHIVED {line} http={code}\n")
                elif code in (401, 403):
                    print(f'SKIP the cloud refused the archive (HTTP {code}); next tick')
                    return
                else:
                    print(f'WARN {line} HTTP {code}')
            if done:
                with ledger_by_key(key) as data:
                    data['archived'] = (data.get('archived') or [])[-(100 - len(done)):] + \
                        [{'session': sid, 'at': now} for sid in done]
            with ledger_by_key(key) as data:
                renames = rename_targets(data, sessions, now, archiving=targets)
            for s, want in renames:
                line = f"{key} {s['id']} «{s.get('title') or ''}» -> «{want}»"
                if args.dry_run:
                    print(f'WOULD_RENAME {line}')
                    continue
                code = rename_session(s['id'], want)
                if code == 200:
                    print(f'RENAMED {line}')
                elif code not in (403, 404):  # another account's session, or not listed yet: the next tick retries
                    print(f'WARN rename {line} HTTP {code}')
        except (OSError, ValueError, ApiUnavailable) as err:
            print(f'WARN {key}: {err}')


# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- self-test

FAKE_CLAUDE = r'''#!/usr/bin/env python3
import os, sys, json, time
log = os.environ['FAKE_CLAUDE_LOG']
a = sys.argv[1:]
with open(log, 'a') as f:
    f.write(json.dumps(a) + '\n')
if not sys.stdout.isatty():
    print('Error: --cloud requires an interactive terminal.'); sys.exit(1)
mode = os.environ.get('FAKE_CLAUDE_MODE', 'ok')
if a and a[0] == '--cloud':
    if mode == 'launch-fail':
        print('Error: no cloud environment'); sys.exit(1)
    n = sum(1 for _ in open(log))
    print('Created cloud session: test'); print(f'Resume with: claude --teleport session_FAKE{n}')
elif a and a[0] == '-p':
    if mode == 'send-fail':
        print('Error: session not found'); sys.exit(1)
    print('Sent to cloud session.'); print('Session ID: ' + a[-1])
'''


def self_test():
    global HEAVY_JOB_BIN
    failures = []

    def check(name, cond, detail=''):
        print(('ok   ' if cond else 'FAIL ') + name + ('' if cond else f'  [{detail}]'))
        if not cond:
            failures.append(name)

    me = os.path.realpath(__file__)
    if not os.access(HEAVY_JOB_BIN, os.X_OK):  # the toolkit layout: heavy-job installed next to this script
        HEAVY_JOB_BIN = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(me), 'heavy-job')
    if not os.access(HEAVY_JOB_BIN, os.X_OK):
        check('heavy-job is installed (the local-guard and preflight checks need it; set HEAVY_JOB_BIN)', False,
              HEAVY_JOB_BIN)
        print(f'\n{len(failures)} failure(s)')
        return 1
    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='cloud-tests-selftest-')
    env = dict(os.environ, CLOUD_TESTS_STATE=os.path.join(tmp, 'state'), CLOUD_TESTS_ALLOW_ANY_REMOTE='1',
               CLOUD_TESTS_OWN_KEY='1', CLOUD_TESTS_NO_PUMP='1', FAKE_CLAUDE_LOG=os.path.join(tmp, 'claude.log'),
               CLOUD_TESTS_LIMIT='none',  # never the real account's usage
               CLOUD_TESTS_API='http://127.0.0.1:9', CLOUD_TESTS_CREDENTIALS=os.path.join(tmp, 'no-login.json'),
               HEAVY_JOB_BIN=HEAVY_JOB_BIN, HEAVY_JOB_DIR=os.path.join(tmp, 'hj'))  # never the real API or slots
    # The throwaway repositories commit with the git identity already configured on the machine (authorship rule).
    env.pop('GIT_DIR', None)
    fake = os.path.join(tmp, 'claude')
    with open(fake, 'w') as f:
        f.write(FAKE_CLAUDE)
    os.chmod(fake, 0o755)
    env['CLOUD_TESTS_CLAUDE'] = fake
    origin = os.path.join(tmp, 'origin.git')
    work = os.path.join(tmp, 'proj')
    sh = lambda c, cwd=work, e=env: subprocess.run(c, shell=True, cwd=cwd, env=e, text=True,
                                                  stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
    ct = lambda a, e=env: subprocess.run([me, *a], cwd=work, env=e, text=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                         stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
    sh(f'git init -q --bare -b main {origin}', cwd=tmp)
    sh(f'git init -q -b main {work} && git -C {work} remote add origin {origin}', cwd=tmp)
    launches = lambda: sum(1 for l in open(env['FAKE_CLAUDE_LOG']) if l.startswith('["--cloud"')) \
        if os.path.exists(env['FAKE_CLAUDE_LOG']) else 0
    sends = lambda: sum(1 for l in open(env['FAKE_CLAUDE_LOG']) if l.startswith('["-p"')) \
        if os.path.exists(env['FAKE_CLAUDE_LOG']) else 0

    tree_now = lambda: sh('git rev-parse HEAD^{tree}').stdout.strip()
    pub = os.path.join(tmp, 'pub')

    def publish(run_id, tree_, code=0, summary='ok'):
        """The runner publishes a result on the results branch (a clone, as the cloud does)."""
        if not os.path.isdir(pub):
            init = (f'git clone -q {origin} {pub} && cd {pub} && git checkout -q --orphan {RESULTS_BRANCH} '
                    f'&& git rm -rqf --cached --ignore-unmatch . && mkdir -p runs')
        else:
            init = f'cd {pub} && git pull -q --rebase origin {RESULTS_BRANCH} && mkdir -p runs'
        body = json.dumps({'run': run_id, 'tree': tree_, 'exit': code, 'duration_s': 61, 'summary': summary})
        return sh(f"{init} && echo '{body}' > runs/{run_id}.json && git add runs && git commit -qm 'cloud-tests: {run_id} [skip ci]' "
                  f"&& git push -q origin HEAD:refs/heads/{RESULTS_BRANCH}", cwd=tmp)

    def ledger_file():
        st_ = env['CLOUD_TESTS_STATE']
        names = [x for x in os.listdir(st_) if x.endswith('.json')] if os.path.isdir(st_) else []
        return os.path.join(st_, names[0]) if names else None

    def ledger_data():
        with open(ledger_file()) as f_:
            return json.load(f_)

    def edit_ledger(fn):
        d_ = ledger_data()
        fn(d_)
        with open(ledger_file(), 'w') as f_:
            json.dump(d_, f_)

    def drain(e_=env):
        """Publishes a green result for every sent run and polls, until nothing is queued or sent."""
        for _ in range(12):
            d_ = ledger_data()
            sent_ = [(r_, x_) for r_, x_ in d_['runs'].items() if x_['state'] == 'sent']
            if not sent_ and not any(x_['state'] == 'queued' for x_ in d_['runs'].values()):
                return
            for r_, x_ in sent_:
                publish(r_, x_['tree'])
            ct(['poll'], e=e_)

    sh('echo hi > a.txt && git add a.txt && git commit -qm init && git push -q origin main')
    p = ct(['check'])
    check('check: no recipe -> LOCAL (3)', p.returncode == 3 and 'no .claude/cloud-tests.json' in p.stdout, p.stdout)

    os.makedirs(os.path.join(work, '.claude'))
    with open(os.path.join(work, RECIPE), 'w') as f:
        json.dump({'setup': 'tools/cloud-setup.sh', 'suites': {'ci': {'command': 'make ci', 'timeout_min': 30},
                                                                 'unit': {'command': 'make unit'}}}, f)
    sh('git add .claude && git commit -qm recipe')
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    check('request: unpushed branch -> NOT_PUSHED (4)', p.returncode == 4 and p.stdout.startswith('NOT_PUSHED main'), p.stdout)
    sh('git push -q origin main')
    p = ct(['check'])
    check('check: recipe and remote -> ELIGIBLE', p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.startswith('ELIGIBLE'), p.stdout)

    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'nope'])
    check('request: unknown suite -> LOCAL (3)', p.returncode == 3 and "suite 'nope'" in p.stdout, p.stdout)

    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci', '--requester', 'test'])
    m = re.match(r'SENT (\S+) session=(session_FAKE\d+)', p.stdout)
    check('request: first run launches the runner -> SENT', p.returncode == 0 and bool(m) and launches() == 1, p.stdout)
    run1 = m.group(1) if m else ''
    log_lines = open(env['FAKE_CLAUDE_LOG']).read() if os.path.exists(env['FAKE_CLAUDE_LOG']) else ''
    check('launch: the brief and the first request reach the CLI', 'corredor de las pruebas' in log_lines and
          'CLOUD-TESTS-REQUEST' in log_lines and run1 in log_lines, log_lines[:200])

    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    check('request: same tree and command in flight -> WAIT, no new launch or send',
          p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.startswith(f'WAIT {run1}') and launches() == 1 and sends() == 0, p.stdout)

    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'unit'])
    m2 = re.match(r'QUEUED (\S+) position=1 suite=unit', p.stdout)
    check('request: the runner is busy -> QUEUED behind it, nothing sent',
          p.returncode == 0 and bool(m2) and launches() == 1 and sends() == 0, p.stdout)
    run2 = m2.group(1) if m2 else ''
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'unit'])
    check('request: same tree and command queued -> WAIT, nothing sent',
          p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.startswith(f'WAIT {run2} queued') and 'position=1' in p.stdout and sends() == 0, p.stdout)

    p = ct(['poll'])
    check('poll: one pending, one queued with its position',
          p.stdout.count('PENDING') == 1 and re.search(rf'QUEUED {run2} .*position=1', p.stdout) is not None, p.stdout)
    p = ct(['status'])
    check('status: shows the queue', 'queued=1' in p.stdout and 'busy=yes' in p.stdout and f'QUEUED {run2}' in p.stdout, p.stdout)

    # The runner publishes run1's result on the results branch (a clone, as the cloud does).
    tree = tree_now()
    published = publish(run1, tree)
    check('fixture: the fake runner published its result', published.returncode == 0, published.stdout[-300:])
    p = ct(['wait', run1, '--timeout', '5', '--interval', '1'])
    check('wait: result on the results branch -> DONE exit 0', p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.startswith(f'DONE {run1} exit=0'), p.stdout)
    check('wait: the queued run was sent as a follow-up once the runner was free',
          sends() == 1 and launches() == 1 and ledger_data()['runs'][run2]['state'] == 'sent'
          and ledger_data()['runs'][run2].get('dispatched'), f'{sends()} {launches()}')
    check('fetch: no local branch created for the results',
          sh(f'git rev-parse -q --verify refs/heads/{RESULTS_BRANCH}').returncode != 0, '')

    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    check('request: same tree and command already done -> REUSE, nothing sent',
          p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.startswith(f'REUSE {run1}') and launches() == 1 and sends() == 1, p.stdout)

    # A result whose tree does not match is not trusted.
    publish(run2, 'deadbeef')
    p = ct(['wait', run2, '--timeout', '5', '--interval', '1'])
    check('wait: tree mismatch -> MISMATCH, exit 5', p.returncode == 5 and p.stdout.startswith(f'MISMATCH {run2}'), p.stdout)

    # A dispatched run past its deadline: the runner is presumed silent, a new one is launched and the run goes again;
    # past the deadline a second time it expires.
    sh('echo 2 > a.txt && git commit -qam two && git push -q origin main')
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci', '--deadline-min', '0'])
    run3 = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('SENT') else ''
    check('request: runner free again -> SENT by follow-up', bool(run3) and sends() == 2 and launches() == 1, p.stdout)
    deadline_min = int(re.search(r'deadline_min=(\d+)', p.stdout).group(1)) if 'deadline_min' in p.stdout else 0
    check('request: the deadline counts from the dispatch (timeout + DISPATCH_OVERHEAD_MIN)',
          deadline_min == 30 + DISPATCH_OVERHEAD_MIN, p.stdout)
    old_session = ledger_data()['runs'][run3]['session']
    edit_ledger(lambda d: d['runs'][run3].update(deadline=time.time() - 1))
    p = ct(['wait', run3, '--timeout', '3', '--interval', '1'])
    e3 = ledger_data()['runs'][run3]
    check('deadline: silent runner -> relaunched and the run goes again (still pending)',
          p.returncode == 75 and launches() == 2 and e3['state'] == 'sent' and e3.get('redispatched') == 1
          and e3['session'] != old_session and ledger_data()['runner']['session'] == e3['session'], p.stdout)
    edit_ledger(lambda d: d['runs'][run3].update(deadline=time.time() - 1))
    p = ct(['wait', run3, '--timeout', '3', '--interval', '1'])
    check('wait: past the deadline a second time -> EXPIRED, exit 5',
          p.returncode == 5 and p.stdout.startswith(f'EXPIRED {run3}') and launches() == 2
          and ledger_data()['runs'][run3].get('expired_reason') == 'deadline', p.stdout)
    p = ct(['record-local', '--suite', 'ci', '--exit', '0', '--summary', 'local fallback ok'])
    check('record-local: stored as local', p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.startswith('RECORDED'), p.stdout)
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    check('request: a local result for the same tree is reused', p.stdout.startswith('REUSE') and 'source=local' in p.stdout, p.stdout)

    # A runner that no longer takes follow-ups is replaced. (The runner of run3 was marked dead: a first request
    # launches a fresh one, then a usable runner refuses the follow-up.)
    sh('echo 3 > a.txt && git commit -qam three && git push -q origin main')
    before = launches()
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    run_a = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('SENT') else ''
    check('request: dead runner -> a new runner is launched', bool(run_a) and launches() == before + 1, p.stdout)
    publish(run_a, tree_now())
    sh('echo 4 > a.txt && git commit -qam four && git push -q origin main')
    before = launches()
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'], e=dict(env, FAKE_CLAUDE_MODE='send-fail'))
    run_b = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('SENT') else ''
    check('request: follow-up refused -> a new runner is launched', bool(run_b) and launches() == before + 1, p.stdout)

    # Rotation after MAX_RUNS.
    publish(run_b, tree_now())
    sh('echo 5 > a.txt && git commit -qam five && git push -q origin main')
    before = launches()
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'], e=dict(env, CLOUD_TESTS_MAX_RUNS='1'))
    run_c = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('SENT') else ''
    check('request: runner with too many runs -> rotated', bool(run_c) and launches() == before + 1, p.stdout)

    publish(run_c, tree_now())
    sh('echo 6 > a.txt && git commit -qam six && git push -q origin main')
    sha6 = sh('git rev-parse HEAD').stdout.strip()
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'], e=dict(env, FAKE_CLAUDE_MODE='launch-fail', CLOUD_TESTS_MAX_RUNS='1'))
    check('request: launch refused -> LAUNCH_FAILED (5), nothing recorded as sent',
          p.returncode == 5 and p.stdout.startswith('LAUNCH_FAILED')
          and not any(e_['sha'] == sha6 for e_ in ledger_data()['runs'].values()), p.stdout)

    # A run the cloud could not prepare (exit 97) is reported, but a new request runs it again.
    sh('echo 8 > a.txt && git commit -qam eight && git push -q origin main')
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    run6 = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('SENT') else ''
    tree6 = tree_now()
    publish(run6, tree6, code=97, summary='setup failed')
    p = ct(['wait', run6, '--timeout', '5', '--interval', '1'])
    check('wait: setup failure reported as DONE exit=97', p.stdout.startswith(f'DONE {run6} exit=97'), p.stdout)
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    run6b = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('SENT') else ''
    check('request: an exit-97 result is not reused -> SENT again', bool(run6b) and run6 not in p.stdout, p.stdout)
    publish(run6b, tree6)

    # Redundant local runs (2026-11-13): a cloud request stops the same suite on the same code that was
    # running or queued in heavy-job, and heavy-job refuses to start it again.
    check('norm: env, bash -c and assignments', norm_command("bash -c 'IS_DDEV_PROJECT=true XDEBUG_MODE=off make ci'")
          == 'make ci' and norm_command(['env', 'A=1', 'make', 'ci']) == 'make ci')
    check('local_match: command, local_commands and equivalent_to',
          local_match({'command': 'X=1 make ci', 'local_commands': ['ddev exec make ci'],
                       'equivalent_to': 'make gate (heavy-job --kind gate)'}) == ['ddev exec make ci', 'make ci', 'make gate'])
    hjdir = os.path.join(tmp, 'hj')
    henv = dict(env, HEAVY_JOB_DIR=hjdir, HEAVY_JOB_SLOTS='1', HEAVY_JOB_LIGHT_SLOTS='1', HEAVY_JOB_SCAN='0',
                HEAVY_JOB_SETTLE='0', HEAVY_JOB_MIN_AVAIL_GIB='0', HEAVY_JOB_POLL='0.2', CLOUD_TESTS_BIN=me,
                HEAVY_JOB_BIN=HEAVY_JOB_BIN)

    def wait_for(cond, seconds=20):
        end = time.time() + seconds
        while time.time() < end:
            if cond():
                return True
            time.sleep(0.2)
        return False

    with open(os.path.join(work, 'suite.sh'), 'w') as f:
        f.write('#!/bin/sh\n[ -n "$QUICK" ] && exit 0\nsleep 300 &\nwait\n')
    os.chmod(os.path.join(work, 'suite.sh'), 0o755)
    recipe = json.load(open(os.path.join(work, RECIPE)))
    recipe['suites']['slow'] = {'command': 'SLOW=1 ./suite.sh', 'timeout_min': 30}
    json.dump(recipe, open(os.path.join(work, RECIPE), 'w'))
    sh('git add -A && git commit -qm slow && git push -q origin main')
    local = lambda e=henv: subprocess.Popen([HEAVY_JOB_BIN, 'run', '--kind', 'gate', '--label', 'local copy', '--',
                                             './suite.sh'], cwd=work, env=e, text=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                            stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
    first = local()
    held = wait_for(lambda: os.path.exists(os.path.join(hjdir, 'slot-0.json')))
    second = local()
    queued = wait_for(lambda: any(n.endswith('.ticket') for n in os.listdir(os.path.join(hjdir, 'queue')))
                      if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(hjdir, 'queue')) else False)
    check('fixture: one local copy running and one queued', held and queued)
    wait_for(lambda: len(subtree(first.pid, processes())) >= 3, 5)
    tree_before = subtree(first.pid, processes())
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'slow'], e=henv)
    run_slow = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('SENT') else ''
    check('request: SENT and both local copies stopped (queued first)', p.stdout.startswith('SENT')
          and p.stdout.count('STOPPED') == 2 and p.stdout.index('STOPPED queued') < p.stdout.index('STOPPED running'),
          p.stdout)
    out1 = first.communicate(timeout=60)[0]
    out2 = second.communicate(timeout=60)[0]
    check('heavy-job: the running copy exits 76 and says why', first.returncode == 76 and 'corre en la nube' in out1,
          f'{first.returncode} {out1[-300:]}')
    check('heavy-job: the queued copy exits 76 and says why', second.returncode == 76 and 'corre en la nube' in out2,
          f'{second.returncode} {out2[-300:]}')
    check('stop: no process of the running copy is left (its sleep included)',
          len(tree_before) >= 3 and not any(alive(x) for x in tree_before), str(tree_before))
    third = subprocess.run([HEAVY_JOB_BIN, 'run', '--kind', 'gate', '--', './suite.sh'], cwd=work, env=henv, text=True,
                           stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, timeout=60)
    check('heavy-job: the same suite on the same code is refused while the cloud runs it (76)',
          third.returncode == 76 and f'CLOUD_RUNNING {run_slow}' in third.stdout, f'{third.returncode} {third.stdout}')
    p = ct(['local-guard', '--cwd', work, '--', 'bash', '-c', 'SLOW=1 ./suite.sh'], e=henv)
    check('local-guard: bash -c and VAR=value forms are the same suite', p.returncode == 3, p.stdout)
    p = ct(['local-guard', '--cwd', work, '--', 'sh', '-c', 'test -z "$(git status --porcelain)" && echo "CLEAN '
            '$(git rev-parse HEAD)" && cd . && timeout 3600 ./suite.sh 2>&1 | tail -40'], e=henv)
    check('local-guard: a suite wrapped in harmless commands (test, echo, cd, timeout, | tail) is the same suite',
          p.returncode == 3, p.stdout)
    p = ct(['local-guard', '--cwd', work, '--', 'bash', '-c', './suite.sh && ./deploy.sh'], e=henv)
    check('local-guard: a suite chained with a deploy is never taken for redundant', p.returncode == 0, p.stdout)
    with open(os.path.join(work, 'b.txt'), 'w') as f:
        f.write('uncommitted\n')
    fourth = subprocess.run([HEAVY_JOB_BIN, 'run', '--kind', 'gate', '--', './suite.sh'], cwd=work,
                            env=dict(henv, QUICK='1'), text=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                            timeout=60)
    check('heavy-job: other code (an untracked file) is not redundant: it runs', fourth.returncode == 0, fourth.stdout)
    os.remove(os.path.join(work, 'b.txt'))
    p = ct(['local-guard', '--cwd', work, '--', './other.sh'], e=henv)
    check('local-guard: another command is not redundant', p.returncode == 0, p.stdout)
    publish(run_slow, tree_now(), summary='ok')
    ct(['wait', run_slow, '--timeout', '5', '--interval', '1'], e=henv)
    fifth = subprocess.run([HEAVY_JOB_BIN, 'run', '--kind', 'gate', '--', './suite.sh'], cwd=work,
                           env=dict(henv, QUICK='1'), text=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                           timeout=60)
    check('heavy-job: already green in the cloud for this code -> refused (76, CLOUD_DONE)',
          fifth.returncode == 76 and f'CLOUD_DONE {run_slow}' in fifth.stdout, f'{fifth.returncode} {fifth.stdout}')
    # Validating a suite (the same tree once locally, once in the cloud) works in this order: local first, to the end
    # and without record-local, then the cloud request.
    sh('echo 7 > a.txt && git commit -qam seven && git push -q origin main')
    sixth = subprocess.run([HEAVY_JOB_BIN, 'run', '--kind', 'gate', '--', './suite.sh'], cwd=work,
                           env=dict(henv, QUICK='1'), text=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                           timeout=60)
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'slow'], e=henv)
    check('validation: local run first (no record-local), then the cloud request -> SENT, not REUSE',
          sixth.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.startswith('SENT') and 'STOPPED' not in p.stdout, f'{sixth.stdout} {p.stdout}')
    for proc in (first, second):
        if proc.poll() is None:
            proc.kill()

    # ---- the queue ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    drain()

    # An old-format ledger (key `runner`, sent runs without `dispatched`) loads unchanged and its runner counts as busy.
    sh('echo 9 > a.txt && git commit -qam nine && git push -q origin main')
    tree9 = tree_now()
    sha9 = sh('git rev-parse HEAD').stdout.strip()
    now_ = time.time()

    def legacy(d):
        d['runner'] = {'session': 'session_OLD', 'created': now_, 'runs': 1, 'brief_version': BRIEF_VERSION, 'kit_sha': kit_sha()}
        d['runs']['legacy-1'] = {'run': 'legacy-1', 'key': run_key(tree9, 'make unit'), 'suite': 'unit', 'command': 'make unit',
                                 'ref': 'main', 'sha': sha9, 'tree': tree9, 'timeout_min': 60, 'requester': '',
                                 'created': now_ - 60, 'deadline': now_ + 3600, 'state': 'sent', 'session': 'session_OLD',
                                 'local_match': ['make unit']}
        d['runs']['legacy-2'] = dict(d['runs']['legacy-1'], run='legacy-2', key='x:y', session='session_ANCIENT',
                                     deadline=now_ - 5)
    edit_ledger(legacy)
    before_l, before_s = launches(), sends()
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    run_l = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('QUEUED') else ''
    d_ = ledger_data()
    check('legacy: a request behind a legacy sent run is QUEUED, nothing sent or launched',
          bool(run_l) and launches() == before_l and sends() == before_s and d_['runs'][run_l]['state'] == 'queued', p.stdout)
    check('legacy: the legacy run keeps its state, deadline and shape; one past its deadline expires without a relaunch',
          d_['runs']['legacy-1']['state'] == 'sent' and 'dispatched' not in d_['runs']['legacy-1']
          and d_['runs']['legacy-1']['deadline'] == now_ + 3600 and d_['runs']['legacy-2']['state'] == 'expired'
          and 'expired_reason' not in d_['runs']['legacy-2'] and not d_['runner'].get('dead'), json.dumps(d_['runs']['legacy-2']))
    publish('legacy-1', tree9)
    p = ct(['wait', 'legacy-1', '--timeout', '5', '--interval', '1'])
    d_ = ledger_data()
    check('legacy: once the legacy run settles the queued one goes to the same runner as a follow-up',
          p.stdout.startswith('DONE legacy-1') and sends() == before_s + 1 and launches() == before_l
          and d_['runs'][run_l]['state'] == 'sent' and d_['runs'][run_l]['session'] == 'session_OLD'
          and d_['runs'][run_l].get('dispatched'), p.stdout)

    # A queued run is superseded by newer code on the same branch; wait follows the chain.
    sh('echo 10 > a.txt && git commit -qam ten && git push -q origin main')
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'unit'])
    run_q1 = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('QUEUED') else ''
    sh('echo 11 > a.txt && git commit -qam eleven && git push -q origin main')
    tree11 = tree_now()
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'unit'])
    m_ = re.match(rf'SUPERSEDED {run_q1} -> (\S+)\nQUEUED (\S+) position=1 ', p.stdout)
    run_q2 = m_.group(1) if m_ else ''
    d_ = ledger_data()
    check('supersede: the older queued run on the same suite and branch is SUPERSEDED by the new one',
          bool(m_) and m_.group(1) == m_.group(2) and d_['runs'][run_q1]['state'] == 'superseded'
          and d_['runs'][run_q1]['superseded_by'] == run_q2 and d_['runs'][run_l]['state'] == 'sent', p.stdout)
    p = ct(['poll'])
    check('supersede: describe() says who replaced it', f'SUPERSEDED {run_q1} by {run_q2} suite=unit' in p.stdout, p.stdout)
    p = ct(['wait', run_q1, '--timeout', '2', '--interval', '1'])
    check('wait: follows a superseded run to its successor (still pending -> 75)',
          p.returncode == 75 and p.stdout.count(f'SUPERSEDED {run_q1} -> {run_q2}') == 1 and f'TIMEOUT {run_q2}' in p.stdout, p.stdout)
    publish(run_l, tree9)
    p = ct(['wait', run_q1, '--timeout', '3', '--interval', '1'])
    check('wait: the busy run finished -> the successor is dispatched meanwhile (still pending)',
          p.returncode == 75 and ledger_data()['runs'][run_q2]['state'] == 'sent', p.stdout)
    publish(run_q2, tree11)
    p = ct(['wait', run_q1, '--timeout', '5', '--interval', '1'])
    check('wait: exit code comes from the final run (0), the old id is announced once',
          p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.count(f'SUPERSEDED {run_q1} -> {run_q2}') == 1 and f'DONE {run_q2} exit=0' in p.stdout, p.stdout)
    check('blocking: a queued run blocks a redundant local run only while it is young',
          blocking({'state': 'queued', 'created': time.time()}, time.time())
          and not blocking({'state': 'queued', 'created': time.time() - QUEUE_MAX_S - 5}, time.time()))

    # A launch that fails inside settle expires the head run and starts a backoff: no launch on every poll.
    sh('echo 12 > a.txt && git commit -qam twelve && git push -q origin main')
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    run_r1 = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('SENT') else ''
    sh('echo 13 > a.txt && git commit -qam thirteen && git push -q origin main')
    tree13 = tree_now()
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    run_r2 = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('QUEUED') else ''
    check('queue: the second request waits behind the first', bool(run_r1) and bool(run_r2), p.stdout)
    edit_ledger(lambda d: d['runs'][run_r1].update(deadline=time.time() - 1))
    before_l = launches()
    fail_env = dict(env, FAKE_CLAUDE_MODE='launch-fail')
    p = ct(['poll'], e=fail_env)
    d_ = ledger_data()
    check('launch failure in settle: the head run is EXPIRED (launch_failed) and the next one stays queued',
          launches() == before_l + 1 and d_['runs'][run_r1]['state'] == 'expired'
          and d_['runs'][run_r1]['expired_reason'] == 'launch_failed' and d_['runs'][run_r2]['state'] == 'queued'
          and f'EXPIRED {run_r1}' in p.stdout and 'reason=launch_failed' in p.stdout and d_['launch_backoff_until'] > time.time(),
          p.stdout)
    p = ct(['poll'], e=fail_env)
    check('launch failure: the next poll does not launch again (backoff)',
          launches() == before_l + 1 and ledger_data()['runs'][run_r2]['state'] == 'queued', p.stdout)
    edit_ledger(lambda d: d.update(launch_backoff_until=time.time() - 1))
    p = ct(['poll'])
    check('launch failure: after the backoff the queue moves again with a new runner',
          launches() == before_l + 2 and ledger_data()['runs'][run_r2]['state'] == 'sent' and 'launch_backoff_until' not in ledger_data(),
          p.stdout)
    publish(run_r2, tree13)
    ct(['poll'])

    # A queued run that never gets a runner expires.
    drain()
    sh('echo 14 > a.txt && git commit -qam fourteen && git push -q origin main')
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'])
    run_s1 = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('SENT') else ''
    sh('echo 15 > a.txt && git commit -qam fifteen && git push -q origin main')
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'unit'])
    run_s2 = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('QUEUED') else ''
    edit_ledger(lambda d: d['runs'][run_s2].update(created=time.time() - QUEUE_MAX_S - 60, queued_at=time.time() - QUEUE_MAX_S - 60))
    p = ct(['poll'])
    check('queue: a run queued longer than QUEUE_MAX_S is EXPIRED (queue)',
          f'EXPIRED {run_s2}' in p.stdout and ledger_data()['runs'][run_s2].get('expired_reason') == 'queue', p.stdout)

    # Preflight: check-only commands before queuing, only when the checkout is exactly the pushed commit.
    drain()
    marker = os.path.join(tmp, 'preflight-ran')

    def recipe_commit(n, **extra):
        rec = json.load(open(os.path.join(work, RECIPE)))
        rec.pop('preflight', None)
        for suite_ in rec['suites'].values():
            suite_.pop('preflight', None)
        for k_, v_ in extra.items():
            if k_ == 'unit_preflight':
                rec['suites']['unit']['preflight'] = v_
            else:
                rec[k_] = v_
        json.dump(rec, open(os.path.join(work, RECIPE), 'w'))
        sh(f'echo {n} > a.txt && git commit -qam recipe{n} && git push -q origin main')

    recipe_commit(16, preflight=['echo style-error >&2; exit 7'])
    sha16 = sh('git rev-parse HEAD').stdout.strip()
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'], e=henv)
    check('preflight: a failing command -> PREFLIGHT_FAILED (6) with its output, nothing recorded',
          p.returncode == 6 and p.stdout.startswith("PREFLIGHT_FAILED ci exit=7 command=echo style-error >&2; exit 7")
          and 'style-error' in p.stdout and not any(x_['sha'] == sha16 for x_ in ledger_data()['runs'].values()), p.stdout)
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci', '--skip-preflight'], e=henv)
    check('preflight: --skip-preflight says so and goes on', p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.startswith('PREFLIGHT_SKIPPED ci (--skip-preflight)')
          and re.search(r'^(SENT|QUEUED) ', p.stdout, re.M) is not None, p.stdout)
    drain()
    recipe_commit(17, preflight=['echo style-error >&2; exit 7'])
    with open(os.path.join(work, 'c.txt'), 'w') as f:
        f.write('not pushed\n')
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'], e=henv)
    check('preflight: the checkout differs from the pushed commit -> PREFLIGHT_SKIPPED and goes on',
          p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.startswith('PREFLIGHT_SKIPPED ci (the checkout is not the pushed commit)')
          and re.search(r'^(SENT|QUEUED) ', p.stdout, re.M) is not None, p.stdout)
    os.remove(os.path.join(work, 'c.txt'))
    drain()
    recipe_commit(18, preflight=[f'touch {marker}', 'true'])
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'], e=henv)
    check('preflight: passing commands ran and the run is queued or sent, with no preflight message',
          p.returncode == 0 and os.path.exists(marker) and re.match(r'(SENT|QUEUED) ', p.stdout) and 'PREFLIGHT' not in p.stdout, p.stdout)
    drain()
    recipe_commit(19, preflight=['true'], unit_preflight=['exit 3'])
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'unit'], e=henv)
    check('preflight: a suite\'s own preflight overrides the top-level one', p.returncode == 6 and 'exit=3 command=exit 3' in p.stdout, p.stdout)
    recipe_commit(20)
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'unit'], e=henv)
    check('preflight: no preflight in the recipe -> says nothing', p.returncode == 0 and 'PREFLIGHT' not in p.stdout, p.stdout)

    # The pump moves the queue with nobody waiting.
    drain()
    pump_env = {k_: v_ for k_, v_ in env.items() if k_ != 'CLOUD_TESTS_NO_PUMP'}
    pump_env['CLOUD_TESTS_PUMP_INTERVAL'] = '1'
    sh('echo 21 > a.txt && git commit -qam twentyone && git push -q origin main')
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'ci'], e=pump_env)
    run_p1 = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('SENT') else ''
    sh('echo 22 > a.txt && git commit -qam twentytwo && git push -q origin main')
    tree22 = tree_now()
    p = ct(['request', '--suite', 'unit'], e=pump_env)
    run_p2 = p.stdout.split()[1] if p.stdout.startswith('QUEUED') else ''
    lock_file = os.path.join(env['CLOUD_TESTS_STATE'], os.listdir(env['CLOUD_TESTS_STATE'])[0].split('.')[0] + '.pump.lock')
    ok_lock = wait_for(lambda: os.path.exists(lock_file) and os.path.getsize(lock_file) > 0, 10)
    pump_pid = int(open(lock_file).read() or 0) if ok_lock else 0
    check('pump: request spawned it (detached, pid in its lock file)', bool(run_p1 and run_p2) and pump_pid > 0 and alive(pump_pid), p.stdout)
    publish(run_p1, sh('git rev-parse HEAD~1^{tree}').stdout.strip())
    check('pump: with no wait running, the queued run is dispatched',
          wait_for(lambda: ledger_data()['runs'][run_p2]['state'] == 'sent', 15), json.dumps(ledger_data()['runs'][run_p2]))
    publish(run_p2, tree22)
    check('pump: nothing queued or sent -> it exits',
          wait_for(lambda: ledger_data()['runs'][run_p2]['state'] == 'done' and not alive(pump_pid), 15), '')
    if pump_pid and alive(pump_pid):
        os.kill(pump_pid, signal.SIGKILL)

    # The account's usage limit (2026-11-19: the 5-hour limit killed the runners and the runs expired). A state dir
    # of its own, so the runs above do not interfere.
    lenv = dict(env, CLOUD_TESTS_STATE=os.path.join(tmp, 'state-limit'))
    lct = lambda a, until=None: ct(a, e=dict(lenv, CLOUD_TESTS_LIMIT=str(until) if until else 'none'))

    def lledger(fn=None):
        st_ = lenv['CLOUD_TESTS_STATE']
        path_ = os.path.join(st_, [x for x in os.listdir(st_) if x.endswith('.json') and x != 'account-limit.json'][0])
        with open(path_) as f_:
            d_ = json.load(f_)
        if fn:
            fn(d_)
            with open(path_, 'w') as f_:
                json.dump(d_, f_)
        return d_

    sh('echo limit > limit.txt && git add limit.txt && git commit -qm limit && git push -q origin main')
    l0, s0 = launches(), sends()
    soon = time.time() + 3600
    p = lct(['request', '--suite', 'ci', '--skip-preflight'], until=soon)
    m = re.match(r'QUEUED (\S+) position=1 .*held_by_limit_until=', p.stdout)
    check('limit: a request while the account is out of usage -> QUEUED and held, nothing launched or sent',
          p.returncode == 0 and bool(m) and launches() == l0 and sends() == s0, p.stdout)
    lrun = m.group(1) if m else ''
    lledger(lambda d_: d_['runs'][lrun].update(created=time.time() - 5 * 3600, queued_at=time.time() - 5 * 3600))
    p = lct(['poll'], until=soon)
    check('limit: a run queued for 5 h does not expire while the limit lasts',
          lledger()['runs'][lrun]['state'] == 'queued' and launches() == l0 and 'held_by_limit_until' in p.stdout, p.stdout)
    p = lct(['status'], until=soon)
    check('limit: status says the account is out of usage', 'account_limit=five_hour' in p.stdout, p.stdout)
    p = lct(['poll'])
    d = lledger()
    check('limit: when it ends the queue clock starts again and the run is launched',
          d['runs'][lrun]['state'] == 'sent' and launches() == l0 + 1 and not d.get('limit'), p.stdout)
    lsession = d['runs'][lrun].get('session')
    lledger(lambda d_: d_['runs'][lrun].update(deadline=time.time() - 60))
    p = lct(['poll'], until=time.time() + 3600)
    d = lledger()
    check('limit: a sent run past its deadline during the limit stays sent; the runner is not taken for mute',
          d['runs'][lrun]['state'] == 'sent' and not d['runner'].get('dead') and launches() == l0 + 1, p.stdout)
    s1 = sends()
    p = lct(['poll'])
    d = lledger()
    e_ = d['runs'][lrun]
    check('limit: after it the cut run stays with its runner and gets a whole new deadline from the end of the limit',
          e_['state'] == 'sent' and e_.get('session') == lsession and e_.get('limit_cuts') == 1
          and e_['deadline'] >= time.time() + (e_['timeout_min'] + LAUNCH_OVERHEAD_MIN + LIMIT_RESUME_GRACE_MIN) * 60 - 120
          and not e_.get('redispatched') and not d['runner'].get('dead') and sends() == s1 and launches() == l0 + 1,
          json.dumps(e_)[:300])
    p = lct(['poll'])
    check('limit: the new deadline is given once per limit window', lledger()['runs'][lrun].get('limit_cuts') == 1)
    publish(lrun, lledger()['runs'][lrun]['tree'])
    lct(['poll'])
    check('limit: a session that carries on by itself after the limit: its result is taken',
          lledger()['runs'][lrun]['state'] == 'done' and launches() == l0 + 1)
    # A runner that stays silent after the limit is a mute runner as before.
    p = lct(['request', '--suite', 'unit', '--skip-preflight'], until=time.time() + 3600)
    m = re.match(r'QUEUED (\S+) ', p.stdout)
    lrun2 = m.group(1) if m else ''
    s2 = sends()
    lct(['poll'])
    check('limit: when it ends a queued run goes to the runner that is still there (a follow-up, no launch)',
          lledger()['runs'].get(lrun2, {}).get('state') == 'sent' and sends() == s2 + 1 and launches() == l0 + 1, p.stdout)
    lct(['poll'], until=time.time() + 3600)
    lct(['poll'])
    lledger(lambda d_: d_['runs'][lrun2].update(deadline=time.time() - 60))
    lct(['poll'])
    d = lledger()
    check('limit: silent past the new deadline -> mute runner: a fresh one and the attempt counted',
          d['runs'][lrun2].get('redispatched') == 1 and d['runs'][lrun2]['state'] == 'sent' and launches() == l0 + 2,
          json.dumps(d['runs'][lrun2])[:300])
    check('sweep: the runner a fresh one replaces is kept in `retired`, so `sweep` can archive it later',
          len(d.get('retired') or []) >= 1 and d['retired'][-1]['session'] != d['runner']['session'], json.dumps(d)[:300])

    # sweep (2026-11-21: 24 replaced runners stayed active in the cloud; one with ⚠ in his sidebar). A ledger and a fake
    # sessions API of their own.
    senv = dict(env, CLOUD_TESTS_STATE=os.path.join(tmp, 'state-sweep'), CLOUD_TESTS_API_FAKE=os.path.join(tmp, 'api.json'))
    os.makedirs(senv['CLOUD_TESTS_STATE'])
    iso = lambda age_s: time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime(time.time() - age_s))
    old, fresh_ = iso(5 * 3600), iso(600)
    sl = {'project': 'sw-1', 'repo': 'o/sw', 'runner': {'session': 'session_CUR', 'created': time.time() - 3600, 'runs': 1,
                     'brief_version': BRIEF_VERSION, 'kit_sha': kit_sha()},
          'retired': [{'session': 'session_RET'}], 'results_seen': None,
          'runs': {'a': {'state': 'done', 'session': 'session_DONE'}, 'b': {'state': 'sent', 'session': 'session_BUSY'},
                   'c': {'state': 'expired', 'session': 'session_RUNNING'}, 'd': {'state': 'done', 'session': 'session_NEW'},
                   'e': {'state': 'done', 'session': 'session_BRIDGE'}, 'f': {'state': 'done', 'session': 'session_OTHER'}}}
    with open(os.path.join(senv['CLOUD_TESTS_STATE'], 'sw-1.json'), 'w') as f_:
        json.dump(sl, f_)
    mk = lambda i, **kw: dict({'id': i, 'status': 'active', 'worker_status': 'idle', 'status_bucket': 'completed',
                               'environment_kind': 'anthropic_cloud', 'last_event_at': old, 'title': 'Corredor de tests',
                               'config': {'sources': [{'url': 'https://github.com/o/sw'}]}}, **kw)
    api = {'sessions': [mk('cse_CUR'), mk('cse_RET'), mk('cse_DONE'), mk('cse_BUSY'), mk('cse_RUNNING', worker_status='running'),
                        mk('cse_NEW', last_event_at=fresh_), mk('cse_BRIDGE', environment_kind='bridge'),
                        mk('cse_OTHER', config={'sources': [{'url': 'https://github.com/o/elsewhere'}]}),
                        mk('cse_STRANGER', title='Cloud test runner')]}
    with open(senv['CLOUD_TESTS_API_FAKE'], 'w') as f_:
        json.dump(api, f_)
    p = ct(['sweep', '--dry-run'], e=senv)
    check('sweep --dry-run: names what it would archive and archives nothing',
          'WOULD_ARCHIVE sw-1 cse_RET' in p.stdout and 'WOULD_ARCHIVE sw-1 cse_DONE' in p.stdout
          and not json.load(open(senv['CLOUD_TESTS_API_FAKE'])).get('archived'), p.stdout)
    p = ct(['sweep'], e=senv)
    arch = set(json.load(open(senv['CLOUD_TESTS_API_FAKE'])).get('archived') or [])
    check('sweep: a retired runner and the runner of a finished run are archived', arch >= {'cse_RET', 'cse_DONE'}, p.stdout)
    check('sweep: the usable current runner is never archived', 'cse_CUR' not in arch, p.stdout)
    check('sweep: a runner a sent run waits on is never archived', 'cse_BUSY' not in arch, p.stdout)
    check('sweep: a working runner is never archived', 'cse_RUNNING' not in arch, p.stdout)
    check('sweep: a runner quiet for less than the grace is kept (it may still publish)', 'cse_NEW' not in arch, p.stdout)
    check('sweep: a bridge (Remote Control) session is never archived', 'cse_BRIDGE' not in arch, p.stdout)
    check('sweep: an id from the ledger on another repository is left alone', 'cse_OTHER' not in arch, p.stdout)
    check('sweep: a session the ledgers do not prove is left alone, whatever its title', 'cse_STRANGER' not in arch, p.stdout)
    with open(os.path.join(senv['CLOUD_TESTS_STATE'], 'sw-1.json')) as f_:
        d = json.load(f_)
    check('sweep: what it archived is written in the ledger', {x['session'] for x in d.get('archived') or []} >= {'cse_RET', 'cse_DONE'},
          json.dumps(d)[:300])
    st_ = json.load(open(senv['CLOUD_TESTS_API_FAKE']))
    for x in st_['sessions']:
        if x['id'] == 'cse_CUR':
            x['status_bucket'] = 'failed'
    with open(senv['CLOUD_TESTS_API_FAKE'], 'w') as f_:
        json.dump(st_, f_)
    p = ct(['sweep'], e=senv)
    with open(os.path.join(senv['CLOUD_TESTS_STATE'], 'sw-1.json')) as f_:
        d = json.load(f_)
    check('sweep: a current runner that failed is archived and marked dead, so the next run gets a fresh one',
          'cse_CUR' in (json.load(open(senv['CLOUD_TESTS_API_FAKE'])).get('archived') or []) and d['runner'].get('dead') is True,
          p.stdout)
    p = ct(['sweep'], e=dict(senv, CLOUD_TESTS_API_FAKE='', CLOUD_TESTS_CREDENTIALS=os.path.join(tmp, 'no-creds.json')))
    check('sweep: without a CLI login it skips quietly (exit 0)', p.returncode == 0 and p.stdout.startswith('SKIP'), p.stdout)

    # Exclusions and slugs.
    check('slug: github ssh alias', github_slug('git@github-work:acme/widgets.git') == 'acme/widgets')
    check('slug: https', github_slug('https://github.com/acme/gadgets.git') == 'acme/gadgets')
    check('slug: not github', github_slug('https://gitlab.com/a/b.git') is None if not os.environ.get('CLOUD_TESTS_ALLOW_ANY_REMOTE') else True)

    class P:  # minimal stand-in
        pass
    saved = set(EXCLUDED_NAMES), set(EXCLUDED_OWNERS)
    EXCLUDED_NAMES.clear(); EXCLUDED_NAMES.update({'private-app', 'team-api'})
    EXCLUDED_OWNERS.clear(); EXCLUDED_OWNERS.update({'team-org'})
    try:
        for name, slug, want in [('private-app', 'acme/private-app', True), ('x', 'team-org/x', True),
                                 ('team-api', 'Team-Org/team-api', True), ('checkout', 'acme/team-api', True),
                                 ('widgets', 'acme/widgets', False)]:
            p_ = P(); p_.name = name; p_.slug = slug
            check(f'excluded: {slug} -> {want}', excluded(p_) == want)
    finally:
        EXCLUDED_NAMES.clear(); EXCLUDED_NAMES.update(saved[0])
        EXCLUDED_OWNERS.clear(); EXCLUDED_OWNERS.update(saved[1])

    shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)
    print(f'\n{len(failures)} failure(s)')
    return 1 if failures else 0


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- main

def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog='cloud-tests', description=__doc__.split('\n')[0])
    ap.add_argument('--repo', help='checkout or worktree of the project (default: current directory)')
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest='cmd', required=True)
    sub.add_parser('check')
    p = sub.add_parser('request')
    p.add_argument('--suite', required=True)
    p.add_argument('--ref', help='pushed branch to test (default: the current branch)')
    p.add_argument('--requester', help='who asks (session id or label)')
    p.add_argument('--deadline-min', type=int)
    p.add_argument('--skip-preflight', action='store_true', help='do not run the recipe\'s preflight commands')
    sub.add_parser('poll')
    p = sub.add_parser('wait')
    p.add_argument('runs', nargs='+')
    p.add_argument('--timeout', type=int, default=3600)
    p.add_argument('--interval', type=int, default=60)
    p = sub.add_parser('result')
    p.add_argument('run')
    p.add_argument('--tests', action='store_true', help='print the per-test lines of the run (outcome<TAB>id)')
    p.add_argument('--grep', metavar='RE', help='with --tests: only the lines matching this regular expression')
    p = sub.add_parser('record-local')
    p.add_argument('--suite', required=True)
    p.add_argument('--exit', type=int, required=True)
    p.add_argument('--summary', required=True)
    p.add_argument('--ref')
    p.add_argument('--run', help='the expired cloud run this replaces')
    p.add_argument('--command')
    sub.add_parser('status')
    p = sub.add_parser('runner')
    p.add_argument('--forget', action='store_true')
    sub.add_parser('brief')
    sub.add_parser('pump')
    p = sub.add_parser('sweep')
    p.add_argument('--dry-run', action='store_true')
    sub.add_parser('self-test')
    p = sub.add_parser('local-guard')
    p.add_argument('--cwd')
    p = sub.add_parser('stop-local')
    p.add_argument('runs', nargs='*')
    argv = sys.argv[1:]
    after = []
    if '--' in argv:
        i = argv.index('--')
        argv, after = argv[:i], argv[i + 1:]
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)
    args.argv = after
    if args.cmd == 'self-test':
        sys.exit(self_test())
    {'check': cmd_check, 'request': cmd_request, 'poll': cmd_poll, 'wait': cmd_wait, 'result': cmd_result,
     'record-local': cmd_record_local, 'status': cmd_status, 'runner': cmd_runner, 'brief': cmd_brief,
     'local-guard': cmd_local_guard, 'stop-local': cmd_stop_local, 'pump': cmd_pump, 'sweep': cmd_sweep}[args.cmd](args)


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
